(function (r) { var P = r.SF2DATA = r.SF2DATA || {}; P.spells = [{"id":"akashic-assistant","n":"Akashic Assistant","fid":"z0Spgrf92nmaqjCW","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You summon a projection of one of the etheric entities that work as librarians and scribes within the Akashic Record to assist your target with a task. The projection appears floating next to the target and doesn't occupy any space. The assistant prepares to [[/act aid skill=occultism]]{Aid} the target as though it had its own reaction. The assistant uses a bonus equal to your modifier in Occultism for its rolls to Aid, regardless of what skill it is Aiding with. On each of your turns, the assistant prepares to Aid its target again. You can use a free action, which has the concentrate trait, to redirect the assistant to a different creature, changing the target of the spell. Otherwise, the assistant keeps aiding the same creature for the duration of the spell.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 bonded creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"akashic-fount","n":"Akashic Fount","fid":"mAu69GVbFKYzQM5a","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You open the target's mind to the Akashic Record to draw in feelings, memories, and knowledge contained within that astral repository. Choose one Lore skill. The target temporarily gains the same proficiency rank in that skill as your proficiency rank in Occultism.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","rng":"500 feet","tgt":"1 bonded creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"anthem","n":"Anthem","fid":"smCC1LNhMb7Z1lrU","t":["concentrate","emotion","focus","manipulate","mental","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You compose the tangle of cosmic melodies into an anthem for your bonded companions. All bonded creatures in the area gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls, and also gain a +1 status bonus to saves against effects that cause Fascinated or Confused.\n\nAnthem","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","dur":"1 minute","area":"60-foot emanation","sus":1},{"id":"cloying-shadows","n":"Cloying Shadows","fid":"rluzzX2ml4yFWnYw","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic","shadow"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You command creatures' shadows to writhe and write and rebel against their owners. Each creature in the area takes 6d6 cold damage.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is Sickened 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes double damage and is Sickened 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The cold damage increases by 2d6.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","area":"10-foot burst","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"data-drain","n":"Data Drain","fid":"CjVOXjuvvTJqC7AD","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You leech memories and conscious thoughts from the target's mind and convert them into astral data that you can record and analyze as easily as if the target's psyche were laid out in ribbons of computer code. This deals 10d6 mental damage with a basic Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage and is Stupefied 1 until the end of your current turn.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is stupefied 1 until the end of your next turn. You Recall Knowledge about the target.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, except the target takes double damage and is stupefied 1 for 1 minute.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The mental damage increases by 2d6.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"eldritch-bond","n":"Eldritch Bond","fid":"Y8Y0LS6sh4pkxPsq","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic","polymorph"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You channel mysterious power from beyond the edges of the known universe to infuse a bonded creature with the essence of an eldritch creature. You grant the target up to two of the following abilities:\n\n- Darkvision\n- Mental resistance equal to half the creature's level (minimum 1)\n- A tentacle unarmed attack that deals 1d8 bludgeoning damage\n- A stinger unarmed attack that deals 1d6 acid damage and has the agile and finesse traits\n- A beam ranged unarmed attack with a range increment of 40 feet that deals 1d6 mental damage\n- 10-foot reach on all melee attacks (including the above)\n- Melee strikes (including those above) affect incorporeal creatures as if they had the Ghost Killer upgrade.\nEldritch Bond\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** The damage dealt by the attacks increases to 2 dice.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** Increase the number of targets to 5 targets. The damage dealt by the attacks increases to 2 dice.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** Increase the number of targets to 5 targets. The damage dealt by the attacks increases to 3 dice.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** Increase the number of targets to 5 targets. The damage dealt by the attacks increases to 4 dice.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"elemental-barrier","n":"Elemental Barrier","fid":"5apI8Yamauo02VYR","t":["focus","manipulate","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"A barrier of protective elemental energy appears around the target, bolstering their defense. Select an elemental trait: air, earth, fire, metal, water, or wood. Elemental barrier gains the trait you chose. The target gets a +1 circumstance bonus to AC. While the spell is in effect, the target can use the Shield Block reaction as if the elemental barrier was a raised shield.\n\nThe barrier has Hardness 6 and 40 HP. It has resistance 2 to one damage type based on the chosen trait: electricity or sonic for air, bludgeoning or piercing for earth, acid or slashing for metal, fire for fire, cold for water, or poison for wood. Unlike a normal Shield Block, you can use the spell's reaction against spells with the chosen elemental trait cast against the creature.\n\nElemental Barrier\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** The barrier has 48 HP.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The barrier has Hardness 8 and 52 HP.\n\n**Heightened (7th)** The barrier has Hardness 8 and 60 HP.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** The barrier has Hardness 10 and 68 HP.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The barrier has Hardness 10 and 80 HP.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","tgt":"1 bonded creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"elemental-nova","n":"Elemental Nova","fid":"DZOjyZBZUrzkw5q2","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"A roaring blast of elemental energy erupts around your targets. Select an elemental trait: air, earth, fire, metal, water, or wood. Elemental nova gains the trait you choose. Elemental nova deals 11d6 damage based on the chosen trait: electricity or sonic for air, bludgeoning or piercing for earth, acid or slashing for metal, fire for fire, cold for water, or poison for wood.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"240 feet","area":"20-foot burst","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"elemental-weapon","n":"Elemental Weapon","fid":"d5dmu4HZ3YyrwcaF","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You create an advanced, martial, or simple weapon out of elemental energy that materializes in the hands of a bonded creature. Select an elemental trait for the created weapon: air, earth, fire, metal, water, or wood. The weapon is tactical grade and comes fully charged and loaded with basic ammunition. It cannot be made of any special materials.\n\nThe weapon has one fewer upgrade slot but can be upgraded with any upgrades you hold in your hands as a locus when casting this spell, which become inert until the spell ends. The weapon deals damage as normal plus 1d4 additional damage based on the chosen trait: electricity for air, bludgeoning for earth, fire for fire, acid for metal, cold for water, or poison for wood.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (2nd)** You can create an advanced weapon.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can create a superior weapon.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You can create an elite weapon.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** You can create an ultimate weapon.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** You can create a paragon weapon.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"3","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 willing bonded creature","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"infusion","n":"Infusion","fid":"d7Mj4nUQe8wg1mV7","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic","vitality","void"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You infuse the target's essence with healing energy. If the target is a willing creature, you restore 1d6 Hit Points. The target is then temporarily immune for 10 minutes. The number of actions you spend when Casting this Spell determines its targets, range, area, and other parameters.\n\n◆ The spell has a range of touch.\n\n◆◆ The spell has a range of 30 feet. If you're healing a creature, increase the Hit Points restored by 6.\n\n◆◆◆ You heal all bonded creatures in a 30-foot emanation.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The amount of healing increases by 1d6, and the extra healing for the 2-action version increases by 6.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1 to 3","rng":"varies","tgt":"1 willing bonded creature"},{"id":"remix","n":"Remix","fid":"Ii8adgcCejAovsNv","t":["concentrate","emotion","focus","manipulate","mental","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You remix the Song of the Spheres into a catchy dance beat. The target becomes Quickened and can use the extra action to Interact, Stride, or Step.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (7th)** You can target up to 6 bonded creatures.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 bonded creature","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"shadow-prison","n":"Shadow Prison","fid":"pgjlPNfXCpEYyLVu","t":["concentrate","emotion","focus","incapacitation","manipulate","mental","mystic","shadow"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You cause memories of the target's resentment, regret, and other negative feelings to engorge its shadow until it grows large enough to swallow them whole. The target attempts a Will saving throw. The target is then immune to this spell for 1 minute.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target resists the spell before it's completely swallowed up, but shadowy tendrils cling to it, making the target Slowed 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target is swallowed by its own shadow until the beginning of your next turn. The target is Invisible and Paralyzed, cannot experience or interact with the outside world, and cannot be targeted by any attacks or other effects.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, except the target is swallowed for 1 minute.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"shadow-snap","n":"Shadow Snap","fid":"uh9Br4yrKvJA6zq0","t":["attack","concentrate","focus","manipulate","mystic","shadow"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"With a snap of your fingers, you beckon the target's shadow to obey you. When you Cast this Spell and the first time you Sustain it each turn on subsequent rounds, you can choose to either attack or stalk the target with its shadow. If you choose to attack, attempt a spell attack roll against the target's AC, dealing 1d10 cold damage on a hit (or double damage on a critical hit). This attack uses and contributes to your multiple attack penalty.\n\nIf you stalk, attempt a spell attack roll against the target's AC the first time the target uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using until the end of your next turn; dealing 1d10 cold damage on a hit. If the attack is a critical hit, the shadow disrupts that action.\n\nEach time you Sustain the spell, you can choose to either attack the target or command the shadow to stalk the target until the end of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The cold damage increases by 1d10.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"shuffle-repeat","n":"Shuffle Repeat","fid":"AlYzxLKWZujnzsjJ","t":["concentrate","emotion","focus","manipulate","mental","mystic"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You shuffle the cosmic mix to repeat one creature's personal anthem, further motivating and empowering them. The target's Strikes deal an additional die of sonic damage and the target gains a +1 status bonus to Will saves and Will DCs.\n\nShuffle Repeat","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 bonded creature","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"vital-rebirth","n":"Vital Rebirth","fid":"MTulATAiOZfZNQ9d","t":["focus","healing","manipulate","mystic","vitality"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"**Trigger** A bonded creature within range would die.\n\n---\n\nYour network catches the soul of a bonded creature before it departs and forcefully resuscitates their body with a jolt of energy. You prevent the target from dying and Transfer Vitality to the triggering ally. The target becomes immune to *vital rebirth* for 24 hours. *Vital rebirth* has no effect if the triggering effect was Disintegrate, Promession, or a death effect. You must have at least 1 Hit Point in your vitality network to cast this spell.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"reaction","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"the triggering creature"},{"id":"vitality-nova","n":"Vitality Nova","fid":"zzi7LUKxKNWr5GsG","t":["concentrate","focus","healing","manipulate","mystic","vitality"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You release a burst of condensed vitality energy, causing a radiant explosion of healing light. Spend any number of Hit Points from your vitality network. Vitality nova heals all creatures in the area 1 Hit Point for every 2 Hit Points spent to cast it. Treat this healing as a use of Transfer Vitality.\n\n- If you spend 20 or more Hit Points and the spell was cast in an area of magical darkness, *vitality nova* attempts to counteract the darkness effect.\n- If you spend 40 or more Hit Points, creatures healed by the spell can attempt a DC 10 flat check to end persistent bleed damage.\n- If you spend 60 or more Hit Points, end all persistent damage on creatures healed by this spell.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2"},{"id":"vitality-web","n":"Vitality Web","fid":"6HMiN0oQzeoYR3it","t":["concentrate","focus","mystic","vitality"],"r":"u","lv":8,"src":"PC","d":"Your network briefly manifests as a web of vital energy connecting members of your bond. Each target gains fast healing 8. When you Cast the Spell and the first time each round you Sustain the Spell, the targets gain 16 temporary Hit Points, which last for 1 round.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The number of targets and the fast healing increases by 1 and the temporary Hit Points increases by 2.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"2 bonded creatures","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"wild-bond","n":"Wild Bond","fid":"ssOpTABjuHAqNTPu","t":["focus","mystic","polymorph"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You tap into the Universal code to infuse the target with the essence of another living creature and grant them one of the following abilities:\n\n- A burrow Speed of 15 feet\n- A climb Speed of 20 feet\n- A fly Speed of 20 feet\n- A swim Speed of 25 feet\n- A Speed of 40 feet\n- A jaw unarmed attack that deals 1d8 piercing damage\n- A claw unarmed attack that deals 1d6 slashing damage and has the agile and finesse traits\n- Darkvision\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** The damage dealt by the attacks increases to 2 dice.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** Increase the number of targets to 5 targets. The damage dealt by the attacks increases to 2 dice.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** Increase the number of targets to 5 targets. The damage dealt by the attacks increases to 3 dice.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** Increase the number of targets to 5 targets. The damage dealt by the attacks increases to 4 dice.\n\nWild Bond","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2"},{"id":"black-hat-trick","n":"Black Hat Trick","fid":"N1Xgt2NVCjCOUyhC","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"You exploit a vulnerability placed into a tech system, then command the creature to do one of following of your choice: Stride in a direction of your choice, attempt a Strike against a creature of your choice with a –4 status penalty, or drop a weapon it's wielding. The target must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target can't Delay or take any reactions for the duration of the spell. Reduce the target's glitching value by 1.\n\n**Failure** As success, but the target must spend the first action on its turn to obey your command.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the value of the target's glitching value isn't reduced.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** You can target one additional creature.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 glitching creature","dur":"until the end of the target’s next turn","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"a-stellar-targetfinder-algorithm","n":"A-Stellar Targetfinder Algorithm","fid":"5kzAMtSSpGDJTIWV","t":["focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"Magitech runes etch onto the weapon's muzzle, guiding the trajectory of your shots unerringly to your target. For the duration, you can make ranged Strikes against creatures that have total cover from you using the target weapon, as long as the creature is within your weapon's first range increment, you're aware of the creature, and you can draw an unbroken path between yourself and the creature. This path doesn't need to be a straight line, and the creature has greater cover against such Strikes. The distance between yourself and the creature you attack is calculated based on the length of the drawn path.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** Increase the maximum distance from which you can target a creature by one range increment.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 ranged tech weapon you’re wielding","dur":"sustained up to 1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"short-circuit-reality","n":"Short-Circuit Reality","fid":"4WIa2Bq7DVgMZfaO","t":["concentrate","focus","technomancer","teleportation"],"r":"u","lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You create a pathway through reality, launching yourself across space to get the jump on a foe. You teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet. Then, attempt a Strike against a creature; you can use your spell attack roll for this Strike. The target is Off-Guard against this Strike.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Increase distance you can teleport by 20 feet.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2"},{"id":"supercharge-synapses","n":"Supercharge Synapses","fid":"4RKn711m9r9Szu0h","t":["concentrate","focus","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You infuse yourself with magical energy to speed up your attacks. You gain the Quickened condition and can use the extra action each round only to Overclock Pulse or Strike.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"force-field-pga","n":"Force-FieldPGA","fid":"1Wp3rkKJQef7K8Tn","t":["focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You gain resistance 2 against one type of damage you took in the last minute. As a single action during the duration, you can change the resistance type to another type of damage you took in the last minute.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The resistance increases by 2.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"magnetic-tuning","n":"Magnetic Tuning","fid":"0rAYoJi9vdj1xIwF","t":["aura","concentrate","focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You amplify the magnetic field generated by your armor's mechanisms, making it challenging for enemies to approach you. You emit a 15-foot emanation of difficult terrain. You and your allies are unaffected by this aura.\n\nWhen you Cast the Spell and the first time you Sustain it on subsequent rounds, you can make a spell attack roll against a creature in the area of this emanation, dealing 3d8 bludgeoning damage on a hit.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The area increases by 5 feet, and the bludgeoning damage increases by 1d8.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","dur":"sustained up 1 minute","area":"15-foot emanation","sus":1},{"id":"supercharge-armor","n":"Supercharge Armor","fid":"0BaSs02dBiL2ASBO","t":["focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You infuse your armor with magical energy to bolster your defenses. You materialize a layer of energy encasing your armor that functions as a superior force field. You then become immune to supercharge armor for 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (7th)** The energy functions as an elite force field.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The energy functions as an ultimate force field.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"jury-rigged-turbocharge","n":"Jury-Rigged Turbocharge","fid":"LwNwSSgQVbF00h7d","t":["concentrate","focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You accelerate and parallelize your thought processes using magic to hack and enhance the inner workings of your allies' tech systems. When you Cast this Spell and the first time you Sustain it on subsequent rounds, the target gains one of the following benefits of their choice (or your choice, if the target is mindless or a minion) for 1 round.\n\n- The target gains a +10-foot status bonus to its Speeds.\n\n- The target gains a +1 status bonus to attack rolls.\n\n- The target gains a +1 status bonus to skill checks.\n\n- The target gains a +1 status bonus to AC and saving throws.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** You can target one additional creature.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 tech minion, 1 willing tech creature, or 1 willing creature wearing or wielding a tech item","dur":"sustained up to 1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"liminal-hyperlink","n":"Liminal Hyperlink","fid":"CmzIZs20jwoaqhzy","t":["concentrate","focus","technomancer","teleportation"],"r":"u","lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You reprogram reality to link together two spaces. Create two hyperlinks in unoccupied squares in line of effect that are at least 15 feet apart. When a creature enters a hyperlink's space, they emerge in an unoccupied space of their choice adjacent to the other hyperlink. A creature that isn't flying treats all spaces lacking solid ground as occupied. If there's no valid space for the creature to enter, then both hyperlinks collapse, and the creature remains in the space where it entered the first hyperlink.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"100 feet","dur":"sustained up to 1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"bonding-charge","n":"Bonding Charge","fid":"Ws85nL9EIkPV07CX","t":["concentrate","electricity","focus","force","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"**Area** variable line\n\nYou supercharge the bond between yourself and your tech minion, adjusting the signal until it physically carries both your magic and the minion's electricity in a shocking display. You Stride, then discharge a line of electricity in a straight line between yourself and your minion. If you don't have line of effect to your tech minion or end your movement further than 120 feet from your minion, this spell fails. Each other creature in the line takes 3d12 electricity damage (basic Reflex save).\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** Increase the damage by 1d12.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"repair-protocols","n":"Repair Protocols","fid":"xNU0CX0Wt0MwOHes","t":["focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You use magic energy to quickly run a number of scripts in parallel that instruct a construct's inner mechanisms to repair themselves with the excess magic power. When you Cast this Spell and the first time you Sustain it on subsequent rounds, either one construct of your choice in range regains 1d8 Hit Points or two constructs of your choice in range each regain 1d4 Hit Points.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The number of Hit Points regained increases by 1d8 if you target one construct or by 1d4 if you target two constructs.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"up to two constructs","dur":"sustained up to 1 minute"},{"id":"supercharge-satellite","n":"Supercharge Satellite","fid":"Is46i6efWR9TqF3e","t":["focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You infuse the target with magical energy to increase its processing power. The target gains the Quickened condition and can use the extra action each round only to Stride or Strike.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"One tech minion you control","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"speedrun","n":"Speedrun","fid":"9Jam9fULcLHFDW32","t":["concentrate","focus","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":9,"src":"TC","d":"You become a flickering echo clipping through the normal parameters of reality. You gain resistance 10 to all damage (except force damage). You gain the cosmic and incorporeal traits, allowing you to phase through walls and move through the air as easily as you would normally walk. You can move through enemy squares (unless they're incorporeal), though your movement still triggers reactions. If your gear is overclocked, you can extend Speedrun's duration by 1 round by making your gear no longer overclocked as you Cast the Spell.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","dur":"1 round"},{"id":"amplify-vulnerability","n":"Amplify Vulnerability","fid":"FfkyvwVrY3sx9NOQ","t":["focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You hack into the fundamental rules of magic that govern your target's surroundings and find a small vulnerability to exploit. The target must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected\n\n**Success** The creature gains weakness 3 to spell damage, and the spell ends the first time the creature takes spell damage.\n\n**Failure** As success, but the spell doesn't end the first time the creature takes spell damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature gains weakness 6 to spell damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The weakness increases by 1 (by 2 on a critical failure).","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"supercharge-prism","n":"Supercharge Prism","fid":"WWkRdbzGnP8nVKIv","t":["concentrate","focus","force","manipulate","technomancer","teleportation"],"r":"u","lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You toss a handful of fragments from used spell gems forward through a tech rune you've drawn in the air, turning them into raw magical energy and shooting that energy forward in a beam. Allies in the area gain 6d6 temporary Hit Points for 1 minute. Enemies in the area take 6d6 force damage and must attempt a Reflex save. If a creature is moved as a result of their saving throw, you determine if they're pushed directly away from you or pulled directly toward you by this forced movement.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and is moved 5 feet.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is moved 10 feet.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is moved 15 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The temporary Hit Points and the force damage both increase by 1d6.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","area":"20-foot line","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"torrent-spell","n":"Torrent Spell","fid":"83y4gDfizNDza0BC","t":["focus","manipulate","technomancer"],"r":"u","lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"**Trigger** A creature Casts a Spell\n\n**Requirements** You have a spell gem with a spell stored that's of a rank equal to or higher than the triggering spell.\n\n---\n\nYou quickly hack into the tapestry of magic another creature is casting. Replace the spell in the required spell gem with the spell that was cast, at the rank and tradition at which it was cast. The spell gem is destroyed during your next daily preparations.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"reaction","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature"},{"id":"accelerate","n":"Accelerate","fid":"RDvWFbAaXtxrhJMD","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","manipulate","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You speed up the flow of your personal timeline in relation to the rest of the universe. You gain the Quickened condition and can use the extra action each round only to Strike, Stride, or Step.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"alternate-outcome","n":"Alternate Outcome","fid":"vL7w8EtvZHlgRKlo","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","misfortune","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"**Trigger** A creature in your quantum field would succeed (but not critically succeed) a saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou reject the outcome for a being in your current existence and replace it with that of a different reality. The target must reroll the triggering saving throw and use the worse result.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"reaction","rng":"within your quantum field","tgt":"the triggering creature"},{"id":"commune-with-tech","n":"Commune with Tech","fid":"dyDIRdq3QmP2QzBR","t":["cleric","concentrate","focus","manipulate"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You briefly establish a mystical connection between your mind and a piece of technology, allowing you to understand the object or manipulate its power. Choose any one of the following effects. An unwilling target must attempt a Will saving throw and negates the effect on a success.\n\n- **Understand Tech** You gain deep understanding of the target object or creature. For the next minute, you gain a +2 status bonus to skill checks to Hack, use, manipulate, disable, identify, Recall Knowledge about, or otherwise interact with the target. Commune with Tech\n- **Discharge Creature** A creature with the tech trait becomes glitching 1 on a failed save, or glitching 2 on a critical failure.\n- **Discharge Object** The object loses all its remaining charges if its item level is up to your level minus 2. If the object is powered by electrical means but doesn't use charges, it instead loses power for 3 rounds. If the object's item level is greater than your level minus 2, it instead loses a single charge or powers down for 1 round.\n- **Charge Object** The object restores all its spent charges if its item level is up to your level minus 2. If the object is powered by electrical means but doesn't use charges, it instead becomes powered for 3 rounds. If the object's item level is greater than your level minus 2, it instead gains a single charge or becomes powered for 1 round.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"one creature or object with the tech trait","save":"Will"},{"id":"forget","n":"Forget","fid":"TAbOBvFU8dLzKiWw","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You force creatures to temporarily forget about the target. The target is Invisible while within your quantum field, and memories of the target are temporarily erased or rewritten. This makes it Undetected to all creatures.\n\nThe first time an enemy attempts to locate the target (such as by Seeking) or uses Recall Knowledge to recall information about the target, they take 8d8 mental damage with a basic Will save as they suffer painful migraines and mental static while trying to process information about the missing target. On a critical failure the enemy is also Confused for 1 round.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d8.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature or object in your quantum field","dur":"10 minutes","save":"basic Will"},{"id":"parallel-forms","n":"Parallel Forms","fid":"XoYUZP9OYdDMz4I0","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","manipulate","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You split yourself into two versions with different fates. Each version of you Strides from your current space, then takes a single action. If the actions are both attacks, they must target a different creature and use the same multiple attack penalty, counting as one attack toward your multiple attack penalty. Each round you Sustain the spell, your parallel forms share actions and use the same bonuses and penalties, including your multiple attack penalty. You apply damage dealt to either form to your current Hit Points, but if both forms take damage from the same effect such as from an attack or spell with area damage, you only apply the damage once. In the case of an effect with a save that affects both forms, you take the worse result and apply it to both forms. When the spell ends, you choose one of the two forms as your actual form and the other version of you disappears. The spell automatically ends if you are reduced to 0 Hit Points.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (8th)** Your parallel forms are Quickened and can use the extra action to Step, Stride, or Strike.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"quantum-analysis","n":"Quantum Analysis","fid":"v8JA4sG2tsVP2gOM","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","fortune","mental","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You see the probability equations all around you, tracing each variable to every possible conclusion. Creatures you target during this spell's duration can't benefit from circumstance bonuses to AC due to cover against your attacks. You also ignore circumstance penalties to the attack roll and any flat check required due to the creature being Concealed, Hidden, or behind cover. You can cast spells that target creatures within your quantum field even if you don't have line of sight to them.\n\nThe first time after casting this spell when you make an attack roll against a creature within your quantum field during quantum analysis' duration, you roll twice and use the better result. This effect has the fortune trait.\n\nQuantum Analysis","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"quantum-negation","n":"Quantum Negation","fid":"d1weVZHIiCXhTlqg","t":["anchoring","concentrate","death","focus","mental","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":10,"src":"PC","d":"You expose a target to a reality in which it's already dead, or never existed in the first place. Once targeted, the creature becomes temporarily immune for 1 minute. The effect of the spell depends on the target's level. If this spell brings a target of level 16 or lower to 0 Hit Points, it ceases to exist in this reality. At the GM's discretion, this may mean it's impossible to restore the target to life without the intervention of a deity, the wish ritual, or similar magic. A target of 17th level or higher merely dies instantly when this spell reduces it to 0 Hit Points, instead of being erased from reality. The target attempts a basic Will save. This spell's damage has no damage type.\n\n**13th or lower** The target takes 9999 damage. It reduces the degree of success of its Will save by one step.\n\n**14th to 16th** The target takes 25d10 damage.\n\n**17th or higher** The target takes 20d10 damage.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"within your quantum field","tgt":"1 creature","save":"basic Will"},{"id":"reality-wipe","n":"Reality Wipe","fid":"YAa1StmuYC2QQ043","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You reset reality within your quantum field, purging the area of all forms of data. All written information and computer data in the area is subject to the effects of Delete. You attempt to counteract any spell whose area or targets are in your quantum field, as Dispel Magic. If the counteract attempt succeeds, it prevents only the portion of the spell inside your quantum field (so if the spell also has targets outside your quantum field, or part of its area is beyond your quantum field, those targets or that area are affected normally).\n\nCreatures in your quantum field take 10d6 spirit damage (basic Will save). Creatures who critically fail are Stupefied 2 for 1 minute.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","save":"basic Will"},{"id":"tech-intuition","n":"Tech Intuition","fid":"A09nTb61ceLF27vX","t":["cleric","concentrate","focus","fortune"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"**Trigger** You attempt a skill check to Recall Knowledge about a piece of technology or to use a technological device, or you roll a saving throw against an effect with the technology trait.\n\n---\n\nFocusing on a piece of technology, you get a brief glimpse of its nature and function. You roll the triggering check twice (or the GM rolls in the case of checks to Recall Knowledge) and use the better result.\n\nTech Intuition","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"reaction"},{"id":"time-loop","n":"Time Loop","fid":"HzFdtjvRCFpb0NrS","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","incapacitation","manipulate","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You trap a creature in a time loop of your creation. The target sees and reacts to a repeating loop of events, based on the result of a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Stunned 1.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Stunned 2.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is Stunned 3 and Slowed 1 for 1 minute.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"within your quantum field","tgt":"up to 5 creatures","save":"Will"},{"id":"warp-presence","n":"Warp Presence","fid":"tZQpEnaFqwmU4AMZ","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"**Trigger** An enemy targets you with a Strike or spell attack.\n\n---\n\nYour presence flickers in the target's mind as though you had disappeared. The triggering creature attempts a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Success** You become Concealed against that creature's attacks for 1 round, including the triggering attack. If you were already concealed, you become undetected instead.\n\n**Failure** The triggering attack misses. You are Undetected to the triggering creature for 1 round. If you use a hostile action, this effect ends after that hostile action is completed.\n\n**Critical Failure** The triggering attack misses. You are undetected to that creature for 1 minute. If you use a hostile action, this effect ends after that hostile action is completed.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"reaction","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"the triggering enemy","dur":"varies","save":"Will"},{"id":"warp-probability","n":"Warp Probability","fid":"KOkGLXwOBAIlczzk","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","fortune","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"**Trigger** You fail an attack roll or saving throw.\n\n---\n\nYou open your mind to read the underlying probability of the multiverse. Reroll the failed check and take the better result.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"reaction"},{"id":"warp-terrain","n":"Warp Terrain","fid":"TN2pHF9l3k4ZJ7di","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You materialize terrain features from another reality within your quantum field. Choose one of the following effects, which lasts as long as your quantum field remains active, until you cast *warp terrain* again, or until you dismiss this spell.\n\n- You cause the area of your quantum field to become difficult terrain. You determine the appearance of the warped terrain. You and your allies can move through the warped terrain normally and can Take Cover using its features.\n- You suppress terrain in your field, turning any existing difficult or greater difficult terrain in your quantum field to normal terrain. This does not apply to effects that cause a creature to count squares as difficult terrain (such as a solarian's graviton-attunement attacks). If you're attempting to suppress terrain created by a spell or other magical effect, you must successfully counteract the effect.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** You can choose to have the quantum field fill with fog, smoke, or another phenomenon that obscures vision. This functions as Mist. You can instead suppress one of these effects within your quantum field.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You can choose to have the quantum field become greater difficult terrain, or suppress greater difficult terrain.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1"},{"id":"warp-time","n":"Warp Time","fid":"1gkdgFwKfAoQx163","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You temporarily alter the timeline within your quantum field. Choose one of the following effects.\n\n- **Rewind** You rewind your personal timeline to an earlier point in your life cycle. You gain 10 temporary Hit Points, which last for 1 minute. Warp Time\n- **Fast Forward** You accelerate the personal timeline of a creature in your quantum field to the end of its natural life cycle. The creature takes 1d10 void damage with a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is Enfeebled 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes double damage and is enfeebled 1 for 1 minute.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** Increase the damage by 1d10 and the temporary Hit Points by 5.","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"1","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"warp-world","n":"Warp World","fid":"9w90nlUdV5HBRWFm","t":["anchoring","concentrate","focus","manipulate","witchwarper"],"r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You recreate a powerful event from another world in your current reality. All creatures in the area must attempt a Fortitude save. The damage and effects caused by warp world are determined by rolling 1d6, as detailed on the following table.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Damage increases by 1d12, persistent damage increases by 1d6.\n\n| d6 | Effect |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Supernova: An exploding sun deals 4d12 fire damage and 1d6 persistent electrical damage. On a critical failure, creatures take double damage and are Dazzled for 1 round. |\n| 2 | Earthquake: The ground shakes, dealing 4d12 bludgeoning damage. On a critical failure, creatures take double damage and are knocked Prone. |\n| 3 | Inferno: A volcanic eruption or firestorm deals 4d12 fire damage. Everything within the aura is Concealed by smoke for 1 round. On a critical failure, creatures take double damage and are Sickened 1. |\n| 4 | Eldritch Storm: A howling tempest of psychic energy deals 4d12 sonic damage and 1d6 persistent mental damage. On a critical failure, creatures take double damage and are Confused for 1 round. |\n| 5 | Flash Freeze: A storm from an arctic planet deals 4d12 cold damage. On a critical failure, creatures take double damage and are Slowed 1 for 1 round. |\n| 6 | Radioactive Blast: The echo of a nuclear reaction deals 4d12 bludgeoning damage and 1d6 persistent fire damage. On a critical failure, creatures take double damage, they take (rank - 3)d6 persistent poison damage and are Fatigued as long as the persistent poison damage lasts. |","trad":[],"cat":"focus","time":"2","rng":"within your quantum field","dur":"1 round","area":"10-foot burst","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"animate-object","n":"Animate Object","fid":"sLzPzk7DJnfuORJ0","r":"u","lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You transform the target into an animated object with a level up to that allowed by the Creature Creation Rituals table and of a type corresponding to the object (so a broom would become an animated broom).\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target becomes an animated object of the appropriate type. If it's at least 4 levels lower than you, you can make it a minion. This gives it the minion trait, meaning it can use 2 actions when you command it, and commanding it is a single action that has the auditory and concentrate traits. You can have a maximum of four minions under your control. If it doesn't become a minion, you can give it one simple command. It pursues that goal single-mindedly, ignoring any of your subsequent commands.\n\n**Success** As critical success, except an animated object that doesn't become your minion stays in place and attacks anyone that attacks it or tries to steal or move it, rather than following your command.\n\n**Failure** You fail to create the animated object.\n\n**Critical Failure** You create the animated object, but it goes berserk and attempts to destroy you.\n\n### Creatures Creation Rituals\n\n| Creature Level | Ritual Rank Required | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| –1 or 0 | 2 | 150 credits |\n| 1 | 2 | 600 credits |\n| 2 | 3 | 1,050 credits |\n| 3 | 3 | 1,800 credits |\n| 4 | 4 | 3,000 credits |\n| 5 | 4 | 4,800 credits |\n| 6 | 5 | 7,500 credits |\n| 7 | 5 | 10,800 credits |\n| 8 | 6 | 15,000 credits |\n| 9 | 6 | 21,000 credits |\n| 10 | 7 | 30,000 credits |\n| 11 | 7 | 42,000 credits |\n| 12 | 8 | 60,000 credits |\n| 13 | 8 | 90,000 credits |\n| 14 | 9 | 135,000 credits |\n| 15 | 9 | 195,000 credits |\n| 16 | 10 | 300,000 credits |\n| 17 | 10 | 450,000 credits |","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"1 object","cost":"rare oils, see Creature Creation Rituals"},{"id":"atone","n":"Atone","fid":"7Fd4lxozd11MQ55N","r":"u","lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You attempt to help a truly penitent creature atone for its misdeeds, typically actions anathema to your deity. If the creature isn't truly penitent, the outcome is always a critical failure. This ritual uses Nature if the target is a druid, and Religion in all other cases.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature receives absolution for its misdeeds, allowing it to regain standing with your deity. It regains any abilities it lost. Before the atonement is complete, the creature must perform a special quest or other task chosen by your deity, as befits its misdeeds. If completed during downtime, this task should take no less than 1 month. For 1 month, the target receives divine insight just before performing an act that would be anathema to your deity.\n\n**Success** As critical success, but the creature gains no special insight regarding its subsequent actions.\n\n**Failure** The creature does not receive absolution and must continue to meditate and redress its misdeeds. Any future *atone* rituals for the same misdeeds cost half as much and gain a +4 circumstance bonus to primary and secondary checks.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature offends your deity and is permanently cast out from the faith. The creature can't rejoin your religion without a more direct intervention.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Increase the maximum target level by 2 and the base cost by 200 credits.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"another creature of up to 8th level who is a worshipper of the same deity or philosophy as you","cost":"rare incense and offerings worth a total value of 200 credits × the target's level"},{"id":"awaken-animal","n":"Awaken Animal","fid":"B4dDkYsHFo1H0CIF","t":["mental"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You grant intelligence to the target, transforming it into a beast. If it was previously an animal companion or minion, it can no longer serve as one.\n\n**Critical Success** The target's Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma modifiers each increase to +2 if they were lower, and it becomes helpful to you for awakening it.\n\n**Success** The target's Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma modifiers increase to +0 if they were lower and it becomes friendly to you for awakening it.\n\n**Failure** You fail to awaken the target.\n\n**Critical Failure** You accidentally awaken the target with a pure bestial hatred toward you. The target's Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma modifiers increase to -2 if they were lower. It becomes hostile to you, attempting to destroy you.\n\n### Creatures Creation Rituals\n\n| Creature Level | Ritual Rank Required | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| –1 or 0 | 2 | 150 credits |\n| 1 | 2 | 600 credits |\n| 2 | 3 | 1,050 credits |\n| 3 | 3 | 1,800 credits |\n| 4 | 4 | 3,000 credits |\n| 5 | 4 | 4,800 credits |\n| 6 | 5 | 7,500 credits |\n| 7 | 5 | 10,800 credits |\n| 8 | 6 | 15,000 credits |\n| 9 | 6 | 21,000 credits |\n| 10 | 7 | 30,000 credits |\n| 11 | 7 | 42,000 credits |\n| 12 | 8 | 60,000 credits |\n| 13 | 8 | 90,000 credits |\n| 14 | 9 | 135,000 credits |\n| 15 | 9 | 195,000 credits |\n| 16 | 10 | 300,000 credits |\n| 17 | 10 | 450,000 credits |","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"1 animal up to the level on the table","cost":"herbs, 1/5 the value on Creature Creation Rituals table"},{"id":"awaken-computer","n":"Awaken Computer","fid":"FIM54CSlkvBwwzdA","t":["mental"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You grant intelligence to the target, transforming it into a creature with the tech trait with free will. If it was previously a minion, it can no longer serve as one. The creature is freed from all orders or programming it previously received. You can create virtual creatures by offering digital media instead of UPBs.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target's Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma modifiers each increase to +2 if they were lower, and it becomes helpful to you for awakening it.\n\n**Success** The target's Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma modifiers increase to +0 if they were lower, and it becomes friendly to you for awakening it.\n\n**Failure** You fail to awaken the target.\n\n**Critical Failure** You accidentally awaken the target with a pure homicidal hatred toward you. The target's Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma modifiers increase to –2 if they were lower. It becomes hostile to you, attempting to destroy you.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"1 computer or tech creature of up to the level on the table","cost":"UPBs or digital media, 1/5 the value on Creature Creation Rituals"},{"id":"binding-circle","n":"Binding Circle","fid":"2ykmAVKrsAWcazcC","r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You call forth an extraplanar creature of a level no greater than double that of the *binding circle* ritual's rank and attempt to bargain with it, generally to perform a task for you in exchange for payment.\n\nYou conjure the extraplanar creature within your circle and negotiate a deal with it. A creature that doesn't wish to negotiate at all can attempt a Will save to stay on its home plane. Most extraplanar creatures feel that they have something better to do than cater to the whims of mortals and require a significant gift, especially if your task poses major risks. Fiends and similarly wicked extraplanar creatures are more likely to accept a bargain for a lower cost as long as it allows them to wreak havoc on the Universe or inflict evil upon the world along the way.\n\nMonetary prices usually range from the cost of a consumable item of the creature's level for a short and simple task to a permanent magic item of the creature's level or more to persuade the creature to fight alongside you. However, some extraplanar creatures may want payments other than money, such as permission to cast a Geas on you to fulfill an unspecified later favor or obtain ownership of your soul via an infernal contract.\n\nYou can add an additional secondary caster to create a warding circle that prevents the extraplanar creature from attacking or leaving the circle during the bargain. This uses the Crafting skill and has the same DC as a secondary check would. This protection ends if you use a hostile action against the extraplanar creature or the warding circle breaks.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You call the extraplanar creature and can prevent it from returning home for up to a full day, potentially allowing you to negotiate a better deal by threatening to leave it in the wards for the duration.\n\n**Success** You call the extraplanar creature and must make your case succinctly, after which the creature can return home at any time.\n\n**Failure** You fail to call the extraplanar creature.\n\n**Critical Failure** You call something vile and horrible, unbound by your wards, and it immediately attempts to destroy you.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"interplanar","tgt":"1 extraplanar creature","dur":"varies","cost":"warding circle ingredients worth a total value of 20 credits × the spell rank × the target's level"},{"id":"call-spirit","n":"Call Spirit","fid":"gsYEuWv04XTDxe91","r":"u","lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You tear the veil to the afterlife and call a spirit from its final resting place. You must call the spirit by name, and you must provide a connection to the spirit, such as a possession, a garment, or a piece of its corpse. A spirit unwilling to heed your call can attempt a Will save to avoid it; on a critical success, a trickster spirit Impersonates the spirit you meant to call. The DC of the Will save is 2 lower if you haven't met the spirit in life. Either way, the spirit appears as a wispy form of the creature you meant to call. Each minute of the duration, you can ask the spirit a question. It can answer how it pleases or even refuse to answer. If the spirit isn't in the afterlife (such as if it's an undead), all results other than critical failures use the failure effect.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The spirit is particularly cooperative, and even if it has strong reasons to deceive you, it takes a -2 circumstance penalty to its Deception checks.\n\n**Success** You call the spirit.\n\n**Failure** You fail to call a spirit.\n\n**Critical Failure** One or more evil spirits appear and attack.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 hour","dur":"up to 10 minutes","cost":"rare candles and incense worth a total value of 500 credits"},{"id":"collective-memories","n":"Collective Memories","fid":"hp6Q64dl7xbdn4gQ","r":"u","lv":7,"src":"PC","d":"You tap into other mortals' memories, knowledge, legends, tales, and lore about a subject. The subject must be an important person, place, or thing. If the subject is present, increase the degree of success of your primary skill check by one step. If you have only vague information about the subject before attempting the ritual, decrease the degree of success of your primary skill check by one step. These modifiers cancel each other out if you have a subject present with little to no baseline information.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** For 1 hour after the ritual ends, you sort through memories that are mostly coherent, emphasizing more accurate or useful information over misremembered knowledge or exaggerated tales.\n\n**Success** For 1 hour after the ritual ends, you learn useful information for further inquiry that remains generally incomplete or enigmatic. As is the nature of mortal memory and stories, you are likely to learn multiple contradictory versions.\n\n**Failure** You fail to learn any useful legends.\n\n**Critical Failure** Your mind becomes overwhelmed with the vast array of knowledge at your disposal. You can't sense or respond to anything in the present for 1 week except to perform necessities like breathing and sleeping. When you recover, however, you can retrain one of your skills into a Lore based on the knowledge of a subject you were accessing, as if you had spent 1 week retraining.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","cost":"rare incense worth a total value of 3,000 credits"},{"id":"commune","n":"Commune","fid":"7DN13ILADW2N9Z1t","t":["prediction"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You call upon an unknown, powerful being to answer questions. The being varies depending on the skill used for the primary check.\n\n- **Nature** Primal spirits of nature, which know about animals, beasts, fey, fungi, plants, topography, and natural resources within a 3-mile radius.\n- **Occultism** Planar and other mysterious entities such as elementals, forgotten spirits, and monitors, which know about forgotten knowledge, the planes, obscure secrets, and other esoterica.\n- **Religion** Divine beings like celestials and fiends that know about the gods they serve and the god's respective purview; these are typically a servitor of your deity if you have one.\nYou can ask up to seven questions that could be answered with \"Yes\" or \"No.\" The entity answers with one-word answers such as \"Yes,\" \"No,\" \"Likely,\" and \"Unknown,\" though its answers always reflect its own agenda and could be deceptive.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You contact a more powerful entity aligned strongly with your interests, possibly even your deity. The entity won't attempt to deceive you, though it still might not know the answers. When it's important to provide clarity, the entity will answer your questions with up to five words, such as \"If you leave immediately\" or \"That was true once.\"\n\n**Success** You can ask your questions and receive answers.\n\n**Failure** You fail to contact an appropriate being.\n\n**Critical Failure** You are exposed to the enormity of the cosmos and are Stupefied 4 for 1 week (can't remove by any means).","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","dur":"up to 10 minutes","cost":"rare incense worth a total value of 1,500 credits"},{"id":"consecrate","n":"Consecrate","fid":"Dbd5W6G8U2vzWolN","t":["consecration"],"r":"u","lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"**Area** 40-foot-radius burst around an immobile altar, shrine, or fixture of your deity\n\n**Secondary Casters** 2, must be worshippers of your religion\n\n---\n\nYou consecrate a site to your deity, chanting praises and creating a sacred space. While within the area, worshippers of your deity gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls, skill checks, saving throws, and Perception checks, and creatures anathema to your deity (such as undead for Pharasma or Sarenrae) take a -1 status penalty to those rolls. If your deity's divine sanctification allows you to choose holy or unholy, you can choose to make the consecrated site holy or unholy as well. If the deity's sanctification *must* be holy or unholy, you must make the site match that sanctification. Strikes made by worshippers of your deity within the area gain the site's sanctification trait, if any.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The consecration succeeds, and it either lasts for 10 years instead of 1 or covers an area with twice the radius. Occasionally, with your deity's favor, this might produce an even more amazing effect, such as a permanently consecrated area or the effect covering an entire cathedral.\n\n**Success** The consecration succeeds.\n\n**Failure** The consecration fails.\n\n**Critical Failure** The consecration fails spectacularly and angers your deity, who sends a sign of displeasure. For at least 1 year, further attempts to consecrate the site fail.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (7th)** The consecrated area also gains the effects of the *planar seal* spell, but the effect doesn't attempt to counteract teleportation by worshippers of your deity. The cost increases to 2,000 credits × the spell rank.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"3 days","rng":"40 feet","dur":"1 year","cost":"rare incense and offerings worth a total value of 200 credits × the spell rank","area":"40-foot burst"},{"id":"create-undead","n":"Create Undead","fid":"c3b6LdLlQDPngNIb","t":["unholy"],"r":"u","lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You transform the target into an undead creature with a level up to that allowed in the Creature Creation Rituals table. There are many versions of this ritual, each specific to a particular type of undead (one ritual for all zombies, one for skeletons, one for ghouls, and so on), and the rituals that create rare undead are also rare. Some forms of undead, such as liches, form using their own unique methods and can't be created with a version of *create undead*.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target becomes an undead creature of the appropriate type. If it's at least 4 levels lower than you, you can make it a minion. This gives it the minion trait, meaning it can use 2 actions when you command it, and commanding it is a single action that has the auditory and concentrate traits. You can have a maximum of four minions under your control. If it's intelligent and doesn't become a minion, the undead is helpful to you for awakening it, though it's still a horrid and evil creature. If it's unintelligent and doesn't become a minion, you can give it one simple command. It pursues that goal single-mindedly, ignoring any of your subsequent commands.\n\n**Success** As critical success, except an intelligent undead that doesn't become your minion is only friendly to you, and an unintelligent undead that doesn't become your minion leaves you alone unless you attack it. It marauds the local area rather than following your command.\n\n**Failure** You fail to create the undead.\n\n**Critical Failure** You create the undead, but its soul, tortured by your foul necromancy, is full of nothing but hatred for you. It attempts to destroy you.\n\n### Creatures Creation Rituals\n\n| Creature Level | Ritual Rank Required | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| –1 or 0 | 2 | 150 credits |\n| 1 | 2 | 600 credits |\n| 2 | 3 | 1,050 credits |\n| 3 | 3 | 1,800 credits |\n| 4 | 4 | 3,000 credits |\n| 5 | 4 | 4,800 credits |\n| 6 | 5 | 7,500 credits |\n| 7 | 5 | 10,800 credits |\n| 8 | 6 | 15,000 credits |\n| 9 | 6 | 21,000 credits |\n| 10 | 7 | 30,000 credits |\n| 11 | 7 | 42,000 credits |\n| 12 | 8 | 60,000 credits |\n| 13 | 8 | 90,000 credits |\n| 14 | 9 | 135,000 credits |\n| 15 | 9 | 195,000 credits |\n| 16 | 10 | 300,000 credits |\n| 17 | 10 | 450,000 credits |","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"1 dead creature","cost":"black onyx, see Creature Creation Rituals table"},{"id":"forge-drift-beacon","n":"Forge Drift Beacon","fid":"ogEFxmaTBlXcpdoS","t":["consecration"],"r":"u","lv":9,"src":"PC","d":"You consecrate a space station to the deity Triune by installing sacred hardware and syncing it to the hyperspace plane of the Drift. It becomes a Drift beacon that allows swifter travel to the surrounding region of space. The ritual requires at least 3 casters (to represent Triune's tripartite nature), but as many as 12 casters have been known to regularly perform this ritual. If the number of casters is not a multiple of 3, the ritual automatically fails.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The forging succeeds, and the entire space station becomes consecrated to Triune, gaining the effects of the consecrate ritual for a number of years equal to the number of casters who performed the ritual.\n\n**Success** The forging succeeds.\n\n**Failure** The forging fails.\n\n**Critical Failure** The forging fails spectacularly and causes a glitch in Triune's code, which might have tangible effects on the space station, like glitch gremlin infestations, a visit from a spectra repair squad, inexplicable technical difficulties becoming rampant, or even planar glitches. For at least 1 year, further attempts to forge a Drift beacon at the site fail.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"7 days","rng":"40 feet","tgt":"1 constructed space station","cost":"UPBs and offerings worth 100,000 credits in total"},{"id":"planar-displacement","n":"Planar Displacement","fid":"HmKajQS0DP23bipp","t":["teleportation"],"r":"u","lv":7,"src":"PC","d":"You draw a ritual circle, and when the ritual is complete, you shift all creatures in the area to a different plane of existence. The skill you use for the primary check must be one that can be used to make a Recall Knowledge check about the intended destination, such as Arcana or Nature for the Plane of Fire or Occultism for the Astral Plane.\n\nA secondary caster can be located at the exact site of the destination, instead of with you at the point of origin. If a secondary caster at the destination succeeds at its check and you roll a success, the ritual is a critical success instead.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You arrive on the intended plane at the last place one of the targets (of your choice) was located the last time the target traveled to that plane. If it's the first time traveling to a particular plane for all targets, you appear at a random location on the plane. The circle remains active for 1 minute, during which time any creature the ritual transported can return to the origin point with a single action, which has the concentrate trait.\n\n**Success** As critical success, but you arrive 1d10×25 miles from your destination.\n\n**Failure** Your attempt is unsuccessful.\n\n**Critical Failure** The ritual fails, and the GM determines whether you travel to the wrong plane or are barred from planar travel for 1 week.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"20 feet","cost":"rare incense, precious metals, and purified chalk worth 5,000 credits","area":"20-foot burst"},{"id":"planar-servitor","n":"Planar Servitor","fid":"vgy00hnqxN9VoeoF","r":"u","lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You call upon a deity (or other divine power) to grant you aid in the form of a divine servitor of your deity's choice, with a level no greater than double the ritual's spell rank. The secondary casters explain what sort of assistance you need and why you need it; if the task is incredibly fitting to the deity, the GM can grant a circumstance bonus to the secondary Diplomacy check or rule that the check is automatically a critical success. If you use the ritual without good reason, the result is automatically a critical failure.\n\nIf the ritual succeeds, you must offer the servitor payment depending on factors such as the duration and danger of the task. Payment always costs at least as much as a consumable item of the creature's level, and often costs as much as a permanent magic item of the creature's level to persuade a creature to fight alongside you. Your offerings should align with the personal tastes of the deity.\n\nYou can alternatively name a being native to the deity's realm that you know personally, with the same level restriction. Such a creature might request something they personally want as payment.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The deity sends a servitor, and the servitor's payment costs only half as much as normal. If you ask for a particular servitor by name, the deity is likely to send that servitor unless the servitor is busy.\n\n**Success** Your deity sends a servitor.\n\n**Failure** Your deity does not send a servitor.\n\n**Critical Failure** The deity is offended and sends a sign of displeasure or possibly even a servitor to scold or attack you, depending on your deity's nature. A deity might also opt to strip divine powers from its followers who participated until they atone","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","dur":"see text","cost":"rare incense and offerings worth a total value of 20 credits × the spell rank × the target's level, see text for more details"},{"id":"primal-call","n":"Primal Call","fid":"pZc8ZwtsyWnxUUW0","r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"This functions as Planar Servitor except you craft a faerie circle and call an animal, beast, fey, fungus, or plant from within 100 miles.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"100 miles","tgt":"1 animal, beast, fey, fungus, or plant","dur":"see text","cost":"faerie circle ingredients worth a total value of 10 credits × the spell rank × the target's level"},{"id":"resurrect","n":"Resurrect","fid":"kqhPt9344UkcGVYO","t":["healing"],"r":"u","lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You attempt to call forth the target's soul and return it to its body. This requires the target's body to be present and relatively intact. The target must have died within the past year. If Pharasma has decided that the target's time has come or the target doesn't wish to return, this ritual automatically fails, but you discover this after the successful Religion check and can end the ritual without paying the cost.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** You resurrect the target. They return to life with full Hit Points and the same spells prepared and points in their pools they had when they died, and still suffering from any long-term debilitations of the old body. The target meets an agent of their deity during the resurrection who inspires them, granting them a +1 status bonus to attack rolls, Perception, saving throws, and skill checks for 1 week. The target is also permanently changed in some way by their time in the afterlife, such as gaining a slight personality shift, a streak of white in the hair, or a strange new birthmark.\n\n**Success** As critical success, except the target returns to life with 1 Hit Point and no spells prepared or points in any pools, and still is affected by any long-term debilitations of the old body. Instead of inspiring them, the character's time in the Boneyard has left them temporarily debilitated. The target is Clumsy 1, Drained 1, and Enfeebled 1 for 1 week; these conditions can't be removed or reduced by any means until the week has passed.\n\n**Failure** Your attempt is unsuccessful.\n\n**Critical Failure** Something goes horribly wrong-an evil spirit possesses the body, the body transforms into a special kind of undead, or some worse fate befalls the target.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You can resurrect a target of up to 12th level, and the base cost is 1,250 credits.\n\n**Heightened (7th)** You can use *resurrect* even with only a small portion of the body; the ritual creates a new body on a success or critical success. The target must have died within the past decade. The ritual requires four secondary casters, each of whom must be at least half the target's level. The target can be up to 14th level, and the base cost is 2,000 credits.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** As 7th rank, but the target can be up to 16th level and the base cost is 3,000 credits.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** You can use *resurrect* even without the body as long as you know the target's name and have touched a portion of its body at any time. The target must have died within the past century, and it doesn't gain the negative conditions on a success. The ritual requires eight secondary casters, each of whom must be at least half the target's level. The target can be up to 18th level, and the base cost is 6,000 credits.\n\n**Heightened (10th)** As 9th rank, except it doesn't matter how long ago the target died. The ritual requires 16 secondary casters, each of whom must be at least half the target's level. The target can be up to 20th level, and the ritual's base cost is 10,000 credits.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"1 dead creature of up to 10th level","cost":"gemstones worth a total value of 750 credits × the target's level"},{"id":"singlemind","n":"Singlemind","fid":"NpsEhi5m9SUm0zqV","t":["mental"],"r":"r","lv":7,"src":"Secrets of the Swarm Adventure Path","d":"You transfer the colony mind ability from yourself and each secondary caster to your target: the entire network of the substance known as \"szandite crystals,\" wherever they exist across the galaxy or on other planes. The material cost of this ritual is destroyed in the process of casting singlemind.\n\nWhen you complete the ritual, if you are within planetary range of one of the Szandite Collective worlds, you lose the colony mind ability, becoming an individual with your own mind. Each of the required Swarm creatures must attempt a DC 28 Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Success** The secondary caster loses the colony mind ability, becoming an individual with their own mind.\n\n**Failure** The secondary caster's mind is rejected by the szandite crystals. They lose their colony mind ability and become a mindless creature.\n\n**Critical Failure** The secondary caster's mind is flooded with thoughts from the szandite crystal network and they instantly die.\n\nAs an additional effect of this ritual, all living non-colony mind creatures in the galaxy who have used szandite crystals to communicate at any point in their lives must attempt a DC 28 Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature gains the colony mind ability. It shares this colony mind ability with all other creatures who gain a colony mind because of the *singlemind* ritual.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes 7d10 mental damage. If it survives, the creature gains the colony mind ability (as success).\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature's mind is flooded with thoughts from casters of the *singlemind* ritual, and they instantly die.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 month","rng":"special (see description)","tgt":"special (see description)","cost":"szandite crystals worth a total value of 300,000 credits"},{"id":"wish","n":"Wish","fid":"6dDtGIUerazSHIOu","r":"r","lv":10,"src":"PC","d":"You weave the fabric of reality itself to grant the target's greatest desire. The target declares their wish in a loud voice at the start of the ritual and again at the end. The target's wish can be anything, ranging from simpler wishes such as vast riches or the casting of a certain spell or ritual, to greater wishes like the destruction of an entire kingdom or ascension to divinity. The GM might decide a wish draws the attention of deities or other powerful creatures, leading to interference with the ritual or attempts to undo the wish. The power of the ritual alters reality to such a degree that even deities can't outright undo the wish, but they can react to the wish by sending servitors to take away the newly acquired riches, for example.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The wish is granted without complication or drawbacks.\n\n**Success** The wish is granted, but with unintended consequences or side effects, such as taking riches from a well-known criminal, stirring a damaged kingdom to war, or angering rival gods.\n\n**Failure** The wish fails and has no result. The GM can instead have the wish be partially granted, but to such a lesser degree that the target will be eternally unsatisfied.\n\n**Critical Failure** The wish is corrupted, resulting in a cruel fulfillment. The GM determines the full results, but the outcome is generally ironic in some nature, such as becoming trapped in an underground vault full of riches, being transported to the kingdom as it's destroyed, or achieving divinity within an inaccessible demiplane.","trad":[],"cat":"ritual","time":"1 day","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"1 creature","cost":"fine ash, magically imbued pigments, and a gem in a marquise cut worth 1,000,000 credits in total"},{"id":"adhere","n":"Adhere","fid":"h7IhypLwItepwhou","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You create a molecular bond between an unattended object you touch (or an object you're holding) and another object or surface that object is touching. Pulling the object free of that surface requires a successful [[/act force-open]]{Athletics} check against your spell DC to Force Open.\n\nIf you instead touch one unoccupied 5-foot square, that surface becomes charged with adhering magic. That space becomes greater difficult terrain.","trad":["arcane","occult","primal"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"1","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 held or unattended object or a 5-foot- square surface","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"analyze-target","n":"Analyze Target","fid":"NkvRoN33RbDg3fl9","t":["cantrip","concentrate","detection","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You focus on the target, gathering data as magical holograms display information. When the casting is complete, you learn biometric information about the target, including its fingerprints, medical conditions, and other basic physiological information. You or anyone you advise about the analysis gains a +1 status bonus to checks to Impersonate the creature, to Treat Wounds on the creature, and to Recall Knowledge about it. If the target is illusory or under the effects of illusion magic, you detect this only if the effect's rank is lower than the rank of your analyze target spell.\n\nAnalyze Target\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** The status bonus increases to +2, and you can target up to 10 creatures.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The status bonus increases to +3, and you can target any number of creatures.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 hour"},{"id":"bugfix","n":"Bugfix","fid":"DyWL7idKpvy3IK5J","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You release a magically self-editing line of code into the target, tackling the root cause of any technical failings afflicting it. You attempt to counteract the glitching condition affecting the target. Regardless of the result, the target becomes immune to *bugfix* for 1 minute.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"30 feet"},{"id":"detect-technology","n":"Detect Technology","fid":"XVPXR4NpkrVw2KjG","t":["cantrip","concentrate","detection","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You send out a pulse of magic that detects the presence of technology, including creatures, hazards, and objects with the tech trait. You receive no information beyond the presence or absence of technology. You can choose to ignore technology you're fully aware of, such as the technology of you and your allies and the ship you're traveling in.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** You learn the level or rank of the most powerful technology, as determined by the GM.\n\n**Heightened (4th)** As 3rd rank, but you also pinpoint the source of the highest-level or highest-ranked technology. Like for an imprecise sense, you don't learn the exact location but can narrow down the source to within a 5-foot cube (or the nearest if larger than that).","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","area":"30-foot emanation"},{"id":"eldritch-lance","n":"Eldritch Lance","fid":"FEaM1B4WuiqFO7Uk","t":["attack","cantrip","concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You condense a beam of mind-assaulting eldritch energy from the dark spaces between the stars and fire it at a target. Make a ranged spell attack roll against the target's AC. If you hit, you deal 2d6 mental damage. On a critical success, you deal double damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature"},{"id":"emoticon","n":"Emoticon","fid":"9nSqaEG9HQB7hMZe","t":["attack","cantrip","concentrate","force","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You unleash a string of emoticons that bash against a creature. Make a spell attack roll against the target's AC, dealing 2d4 bludgeoning or force damage (chosen when you Cast the Spell).\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d4.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature"},{"id":"implant-data","n":"Implant Data","fid":"ZBeKxBcUOsXrfMRo","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You reprogram a computer or device to display a chosen piece of data when accessed. You can implant up to one piece of data per spell rank. A piece of data can be a simple fact, such as a creature or object's location or physical description; an image of a creature or object; or a simple statement of no more than 300 characters. When the target computer or device is accessed, this implanted data is the first data the accessing creature gains, regardless of what data the creature is looking for. Implanted data doesn't prevent a creature from accessing other information stored on a device, change how the device functions, or otherwise inhibit the device from functioning. If this spell's duration ends before a creature accesses the implanted data, the information vanishes.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** The duration is one year.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The duration is unlimited.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 computer","dur":"1 day"},{"id":"injury-echo","n":"Injury Echo","fid":"sNUvbMoMeLTnYJm8","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You manifest an injury from the future or past to harm a creature in the present. Choose bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage. The target takes 1d8 of the selected damage type with a basic Will save. If the target fails its save and then takes the same type of damage before the end of your next turn, it takes an additional ceil((item level)/2)d4 persistent bleed damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The initial damage increases by 1d8, and the persistent damage on a failure increases by 1d4.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"basic Will"},{"id":"linked-sight","n":"Linked Sight","fid":"MdtOuzzLWcG0CD60","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate","scrying"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You toss the required locus to a point in range, imbuing the optic tool with a connection to your own vision. For the duration, the locus can see in all directions with your normal visual senses, though it treats sight as an imprecise sense past 15 feet. You can Sustain the spell to switch between seeing through the locus or through your standard vision.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The duration of the spell is increased by 5 minutes, and the range past which the locus's sight becomes imprecise is increased by 5 feet.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","dur":"5 minutes"},{"id":"measure","n":"Measure","fid":"bBQ83xDvjQS3W1CG","t":["cantrip","concentrate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You learn the approximate measurements (length, width, depth, height, and weight) of creatures and objects you can observe in the area. If an object or creature extends out of the area, you learn only the measurements within the area, but nothing about what you can't observe. For example, you can't determine the thickness or weight of a wall you can observe only one side of, or the depth of water that extends beyond the spell's range. Each time you Sustain the spell, you learn the exact measurements of one creature or object in the area, including imprecisions or anomalies that might indicate structural weakness. Magically altered targets give you information that reflects what you observe rather than accurate measurements.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Extend the range of measure by 100 feet.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","area":"200-foot emanation","sus":1},{"id":"recharge-weapon","n":"Recharge Weapon","fid":"5y70IWhVV6bVjC9N","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You touch a weapon with no remaining ammunition and recharge it with magical energy. The target gains ammunition or charges equal to its expend until the end of your next turn, allowing anyone holding the target to make one Strike with the weapon. This spell only recharges weapons that use ammunition with a cost of 10 credits or less.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** The target gains ammunition or charges equal to double its expend.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The target gains ammunition or charges equal to triple its expend.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The target gains ammunition or charges equal to quadruple its expend.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"1","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 weapon with capacity"},{"id":"reorient","n":"Reorient","fid":"t0oFlhMhNOHbb6rG","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate","vitality"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"Applying a combination of vital energy and acupressure, you help the target regain its footing. The target loses the Off-Guard condition if it has it. The target becomes immune to the off-guard condition until the start of your next turn, even if the condition would be circumstantially applied, such as by being flanked or Prone. The target is then immune to reorient for 10 minutes.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"1","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature"},{"id":"scan-environment","n":"Scan Environment","fid":"nf8q0zvJDnnkzANe","t":["cantrip","concentrate","exploration","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You analyze the natural environment in the area within 1 mile, learning general information about the atmosphere, biomes, and gravity. You forecast the weather for the next hour, including the direction it will come from; learn which atmospheres, biomes, and gravity are in the area, as well as the direction and distance to those elements; and learn if anything in the area presents an environmental hazard, including cold or heat dangers (at what temperature range), radiation (at what severity), smoke effects, and underwater conditions. This is enough to detect large effects that span spaces over 30 feet in diameter only. You gain a general sense of where and how far away these dangers are.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The scanned area increases in radius by 1 mile.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"10 minutes"},{"id":"seek-the-stars","n":"Seek the Stars","fid":"3VucgRc8FRPGy9NI","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"In your mind's eye, you chart a path through the cosmos. If you're in Pact Worlds space, you immediately know which direction to travel in order to reach the Starstone on Absalom Station. If you're outside the Pact System, you know the direction to the nearest Drift beacon or the Starstone.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (7th)** You can instead know the direction to a familiar location, such as a world or way station you've visited.","trad":["divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2"},{"id":"stumble","n":"Stumble","fid":"jgN33YSYXB8iIHTw","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"A burst of microgravity causes a tremor around the target, pulling it toward the ground. The target must attempt a Reflex save.\n\n---\n\n**Failure** The target becomes Off-Guard for 1 round. If the target was flying, swimming, or floating, it falls 10 feet downward.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target falls Prone. If the target was flying, swimming, or floating, it falls 20 feet downward.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** If the target falls, it falls an additional 5 feet on a failure and 10 feet on a critical failure.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"100 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"summon-instrument","n":"Summon Instrument","fid":"yvs1zN5Pai5U4CJX","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You materialize a handheld Musical Instrument (Handheld, Commercial) in your grasp. The instrument is typical for its type, but it plays for only you. It vanishes when the spell ends. If you cast summon instrument again, any instrument you previously summoned disappears.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** The instrument is instead a Musical Instrument (Handheld, Tactical).","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"3","dur":"1 hour"},{"id":"vague-idea","n":"Vague Idea","fid":"8FT564z5zMQVZNih","t":["cantrip","manipulate","mental"],"lv":1,"src":"Guilt of the Grave World Player's Guide","d":"You jog your own memory, or that of a nearby creature, helping them remember a bit of information at the cost of some of their visual acuity. A willing target may intentionally choose to take the effects of a failed saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Dazzled until the end of its next turn, but receives a +1 circumstance bonus on all checks to Recall Knowledge until the end of its next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (4th)** The circumstance bonus increases to +2.\n\n**Heightened (7th)** The circumstance bonus increases to +3.\n\n**Heightened (10th)** The circumstance bonus increases to +4.\n\nVague Idea","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"adaptive-camouflage","n":"Adaptive Camouflage","fid":"p83iYWlcJRqe0PxL","t":["illusion","manipulate","subtle"],"r":"u","lv":1,"src":"SFS","d":"**Trigger** You are caught in the area of a hostile effect.\n\n---\n\nThis magic takes advantage of disorienting explosions and gunfire to give its caster an opportunity to hide. You become undetected to all creatures that rely on visual senses unless they can see Invisible creatures. You Step. If you have cover, greater cover, or concealment, attempt a Stealth check to Hide. The invisibility then ends, and you either become observed or Hidden to creatures as determined by your check to Hide, if you made one. If you remain in the area of the trigger, you gain a +2 status bonus to this Stealth check. If you are no longer in the area of the trigger, you gain a +2 status bonus to your Reflex save (if any) against the triggering effect.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"reaction"},{"id":"akashic-download","n":"Akashic Download","fid":"VynaowCerc7B4yvI","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You execute a psychic search of the Akashic Record for information about a specific topic and magically transfer this data to your comm unit or computer. When you Cast this Spell, choose any skill in which you're trained that has the Recall Knowledge action.\n\nAny time during the duration, you can consult your comm unit while attempting a Recall Knowledge check using your chosen skill. This check gains a +1 status bonus. Checking your comm unit is part of the action to Recall Knowledge. You must be holding the comm unit to do so. The comm unit instantly compiles and displays snippets and selections from various media relevant to the topic, which grants you the bonus. If you roll a critical failure on this check, you get a failure instead. If the check is successful and the subject is a creature, you gain additional information or context about the creature. Once you reference the comm unit, the spell ends. When the spell ends, your access to the Akashic Record ends, and all the information you downloaded returns to the Akashic Record.\n\nAkashic Download\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** You can reference your comm unit three times before the spell ends.","trad":["occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","dur":"1 day"},{"id":"alchemical-shot","n":"Alchemical Shot","fid":"j25dWcmRG1vv5DJc","t":["concentrate","manipulate","metal"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You transmute scrap metal into a shotgun blast of high-purity precious metals. Creatures in the area take 1d8 piercing damage with a basic Reflex save. The damage counts as cold iron or silver (chosen when you Cast the Spell). The spell gains no benefits from the chosen material except for determining immunities, resistances, and weaknesses.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** The damage increases to 3d8.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** The damage increases to 6d8, and you can also choose to have the damage count as adamantine, cold iron, or silver.\n\n**Heightened (7th)** As 5th-rank, and increase the damage to 9d8.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The damage increases to 12d8, and you can choose to have the damage count as any precious metal.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","area":"15-foot cone","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"cellular-stimulant","n":"Cellular Stimulant","fid":"QiW8VNdBf0SFUq69","t":["concentrate","manipulate","vitality"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You vitalize and stimulate the target at a cellular level, giving it a temporary burst of energy that unfortunately takes an exhausting toll. The target gains the Quickened condition and can use the extra action to Stride or Strike. After that round ends, the target becomes Fatigued until it can rest for 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You can target up to six creatures by using 2 actions to Cast this Spell.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"1","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 willing living creature that isn't fatigued or quickened","dur":"1 round"},{"id":"chill-gaze","n":"Chill Gaze","fid":"JIAIyvj4PV84tnFk","t":["cold","concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"lv":1,"src":"Guilt of the Grave World","d":"Your eyes turn an icy blue color as the temperature in the area drops. Your cold, hard gaze literally chills the air around your foe's body, making it harder for them to move. When you cast chill gaze, choose clumsy or enfeebled. Your foe takes effects depending on your choice, based on the result of its saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Clumsy 1 or Enfeebled 1 (depending on your choice) for the duration of the spell.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the target is Clumsy 2 or Enfeebled 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (4th)** You can target up to five creatures.\n\n**Heightened (7th)** You can target up to ten creatures.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Fortitude","sus":1},{"id":"comfortmoji","n":"Comfortmoji","fid":"jChXPibVLmIC9QaE","t":["concentrate","healing","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"An emoji of a bandage covers the target, granting it fast healing 2 for the duration or until it removes the bandage, whichever comes first. The target or an ally (if the target is willing) can Interact to remove the bandage and apply it to another adjacent creature, transferring the spell's benefits to the new creature. This does not reset the spell's duration.\n\nComfortmoji\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The fast healing increases by 2.","trad":["occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"crymoji","n":"Crymoji","fid":"eChIzJ8Zvcmd6HWs","t":["concentrate","manipulate","water"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You create an emoji that's crying so hard that it spreads water around itself, whether from laughter or sadness. When a creature starts to Stride in the area the first time each turn, it must succeed at a Reflex saving throw or fall Prone and take 1d6 bludgeoning damage, disrupting the movement. Each time you Sustain the spell, the area increases by 5 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"10-foot burst","save":"Reflex","sus":1},{"id":"delete","n":"Delete","fid":"yXD9uU8w8uFD2OBQ","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You delete data from a device or object with a flamboyant magical gesture. This data might be handwritten, printed, or digital. You delete up to 1,500 words' worth of text, one page of content, or one display screen worth of text or other visual information. Non-magical writing in or on an unattended or held object is automatically deleted. Attempt a counteract check to delete digital or magical writing. If you fail to delete writing that's part of a hazard, you trigger the hazard. This can't be used to delete the contents of a spellbook or similar means of storing magical formulas or spells.\n\nIf you target an attended tech item with the tracking trait, attempt a counteract check. On a success, the item becomes glitching 1. A creature holding the item can Interact to restart the software, reducing the glitching value by 1.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (7th)** You can delete all the data stored locally on a single device or book, or all the data on a device or book related to a specific name, topic, or category.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 dataset or tech item with the tracking trait"},{"id":"dream-of-home","n":"Dream of Home","fid":"ZrFj6ktotd0pBnqO","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental","subtle"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You draw on a creature's thoughts of home and the comfort it finds in that concept, overwhelming the creature with wistful memories of whatever home means to it. The target must succeed at a Will save or become Fascinated by the memories.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Will","sus":1},{"id":"emoji-spray","n":"Emoji Spray","fid":"HmiwNtwDnfRKGrSI","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You unleash a cone of thematic emojis. Choose a type of emoji you spray, which determines the effects of the spell. Each creature in the area experiences the chosen effect.\n\n- **Eye Emojis** Bright eyes cling to the creature, which must attempt a Fortitude save. Emoji spray gains the light and visual traits.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is distracted by the light, becoming Off-Guard until the start of your next turn.\n\n**Failure** As success, but the creature can't benefit from the Concealed condition and takes a –2 circumstance penalty to Stealth checks to [[/act hide]] for as long as it's off-guard.\n\n- **Food Emojis** Food gets into the creature's circuits. The creature must succeed at a Reflex save or the creature and one tech item of your choice that it's holding becomes Glitching 1 (Glitching 2 on a critical failure).\n\n- **Grawlix Emojis** Symbols representing profanity barrage the creature, dealing 2d4 mental damage (basic Will save); on a failure, it also becomes Stupefied 1 (Stupefied 3 on a critical failure). Emoji spray gains the mental trait.\n\n- **Weapon Emojis** Swords and daggers pierce the creature, dealing 1d6 persistent bleed damage (basic Reflex save) as the weapons tear into it.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The mental damage increases by 2d4, and the persistent bleed damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"15-foot cone"},{"id":"enhance-body","n":"Enhance Body","fid":"GmeI009NbLbR6sR5","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You infuse the target's body with magic power. All its unarmed attacks gain the tracking +1 trait, and increase the number of weapon damage dice to two.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The unarmed attacks gain the tracking +2 trait, and increase the number of weapon damage dice to three.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The unarmed attacks gain the tracking +3 trait, and increase the number of weapon damage dice to four.\n\nEnhance Body","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 willing creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"enhance-weapon","n":"Enhance Weapon","fid":"ahXTkKpQtOTAQOFm","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You infuse the weapon with magic allowing it to safely operate beyond its normal parameters. If the target is a commercial or tactical weapon, it becomes an advanced weapon, gaining a +1 item bonus to attack rolls and increasing the number of weapon damage dice to two.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** If the target is a commercial, tactical, advanced, or superior weapon, it becomes an elite weapon, gaining a +2 item bonus to attack rolls and increasing the number of weapon damage dice to three.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The target becomes a paragon weapon, gaining a +3 to item bonus to attack rolls and increasing the number of weapon damage dice to four.\n\nEnhance Weapon","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 weapon that is unattended or wielded by a willing creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"exhale-toxins","n":"Exhale Toxins","fid":"9jZ8lah3VMO7iYW8","t":["concentrate","manipulate","poison"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You release all the built-up toxins in the locus at once, exhaling a poisonous mist. Creatures in the area take 2d4 poison damage and must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Sickened 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is Sickened 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d4.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"15-foot cone","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"glow-up","n":"Glow Up","fid":"V1cojmrEOWkJ1yPF","t":["concentrate","illusion","manipulate","visual"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You create an illusion that causes the target to appear more charming and genteel to observers. The spell accentuates the target's appearance, clothing, voice, and mannerisms according to what an observer finds appealing. Held items are unaffected, and any worn item removed from the creature returns to its true appearance.\n\nThe target gains a +1 status bonus to Diplomacy checks to Make an Impression and lets the target add its level to Diplomacy checks if untrained. In addition, the target can attempt a Diplomacy check to Gather Information in only 10 minutes. You can Dismiss this spell.\n\nGlow Up\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The bonus increases by 1, to a maximum of +4 at 7th rank.","trad":["arcane","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 willing creature","dur":"1 hour"},{"id":"junk-armor","n":"Junk Armor","fid":"oSFO8npwL2vKDdxm","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You create light, medium, or heavy armor out of junk that you immediately don. You lose the benefits of any armor you were already wearing when you cast this spell, including any upgrades in that armor. You can create any common commercial grade armor, and it gains the noisy and tech traits if it doesn't have them already. It can't be made of any special materials.\n\nThe armor has one fewer upgrade slot than usual. When you Cast this Spell, you can automatically Install any upgrades you're holding in your hands as a locus into any upgrade slots the armor has.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (2nd)** You can create tactical armor.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can create advanced armor.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You can create superior armor.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** You can create elite armor.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** You can create ultimate armor.\n\n**Heightened (10th)** You can create paragon armor.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"junk-grenade","n":"Junk Grenade","fid":"tETsnyXOafzISpKO","t":["concentrate","junk","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You coalesce junk together to make an improvised explosive device. You create a commercial grade grenade in your hand, the hand of an adjacent ally, or on the ground in adjacent square. Choose the type of grenade when you Cast the Spell, using the following list: electromag grenade, flash grenade, frag grenade, glitterbomb, incendiary grenade, or smoke grenade. The Reflex save for this grenade uses your spell DC instead of your class DC.\n\nJunk Grenade\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (2nd)** You can create a tactical grenade.\n\n**Heightened (4th)** You can create an advanced grenade.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can create a superior grenade.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You can create an elite grenade.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** You can create an ultimate grenade.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** You can create a paragon grenade.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"junk-restraints","n":"Junk Restraints","fid":"kPp8vbT1R5afbOux","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"Pieces of junk clamp around the target's limbs, locking them in place like a series of makeshift manacles. The target must attempt a Reflex saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Suppressed for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Clumsy 1 and suppressed for 1 hour.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the creature is also Restrained and drops all items it's holding in its space. The restraints' [[/act force-open]] and [[/act escape]] DCs are equal to your spell DC. A creature can attack the restraints in an attempt to break its grip. The restraints have AC equal to your spell DC, Hardness 5, and 20 Hit Points. Destroying, Forcing Open, or Escaping from the restraints ends the spell.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** The junk has Hardness 8 and 66 Hit Points.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** The junk has Hardness 8 and 88 Hit Points.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** The junk has Hardness 10 and 100 Hit Points.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"junk-weapon","n":"Junk Weapon","fid":"amWAlEKTNuBAgj5m","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"Junk comes flying together to form a temporary weapon. You create a common advanced, martial, or simple weapon in your hands, the hands of an adjacent ally, or on the ground in an adjacent square. The weapon is commercial grade and comes fully charged with a default battery and loaded with basic ammunition or chem. It can't be made of any special materials.\n\nThe weapon has one fewer upgrade slot than usual. When you Cast this Spell, you can automatically Install any upgrades you are holding in your hands as a locus into any upgrade slots the weapon has. When you Interact to stow the *junk weapon*, you can collapse it into an unassuming accessory on one of your limbs, such as a bracelet or glove made out of junk.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (2nd)** You can create a tactical weapon.\n\n**Heightened (4th)** You can create an advanced.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can create a superior weapon.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You can create an elite weapon.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** You can create an ultimate weapon.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** You can create a paragon weapon.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"junkbot","n":"Junkbot","fid":"X7HA6V2phMsaFce3","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You shape nearby junk into a minibot of 1st level or lower whose formula you used as this spell's locus. Activate the Minibot. If the locus is a handheld tech item, such as a comm unit, you can use it to install any electronic storage necessary for the minibot to function, such as songs in a beatbot or storage for a camerabot. When the spell ends, the minibot turns into a pile of junk\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** You create a minibot up to 2nd level.\n\n**Heightened (4th)** You create a minibot up to 4th level.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You create a minibot up to 8th level.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You create a minibot up to 12th level.\n\n**Heightened (7th)** You create a minibot up to 14th level.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","dur":"1 hour"},{"id":"junkify","n":"Junkify","fid":"WYzRscCSsB8wT6Aq","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You corrode a useful piece of tech into obsolete junk. The target takes 1d8 acid damage, with a basic Reflex save if the target is a creature or by a creature holding or wielding the target. The target becomes Glitching 2 on a failure (or if unattended). If this damage reduces the target to 0 Hit Points, it becomes junk, and as long as it's unattended, any space it occupies becomes difficult terrain.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** Increase the damage by 1d8 and the glitching condition by 1.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 construct, item, or object that's made of metal or that has the tech trait","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"lock","n":"Lock","fid":"Azoh0BSoCASrA1lr","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"The target's latch mechanism clinks shut, held fast by unseen magical wards. When you magically lock a target, you set an Athletics and Thievery DC to open it equal to your spell DC or the base lock DC with a +4 status bonus, whichever is higher. Any key or combination that once opened a lock affected by this spell does not do so for the duration of the spell, though the key or combination does grant a +4 circumstance bonus to checks to open the door. If the target is opened, the spell ends. Assuming the target is not barred or locked in some additional way, you can unlock and open it with an Interact action during which you touch the target. This does not end the spell. You can Dismiss this spell at any time and from any distance.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (2nd)** The duration is unlimited, but you must expend 60 credits worth of precious metals as an additional cost.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 lock, or a door or container with a latch","dur":"until your next daily preparations"},{"id":"mind-skewer","n":"Mind Skewer","fid":"uBo6g5aW087cLSJR","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You overload a creature's mind with a glut of psychic information or divine judgments. The mental onslaught deals 2d6 mental damage. On a critical failure, the target is also Stupefied 2 for 1 round.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"basic Will"},{"id":"motivating-ringtone","n":"Motivating Ringtone","fid":"5ZZca1GGJs44OxC8","t":["auditory","concentrate","emotion","healing","manipulate","subtle"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You cause the target comm unit to play a cosmically composed personal theme song specific to its owner. The creature who owns the target comm unit regains 1d8+4 Hit Points when you Cast the Spell, a +5-foot status bonus to all Speeds, and a +1 status bonus to saves against fear effects for the duration as long as the comm unit continues to play the ringtone.\n\nMotivating Ringtone\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The amount of healing increases by 1d8+4.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 comm unit","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"nanite-snipe","n":"Nanite Snipe","fid":"IKoJFpftmymU0JxI","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"Make a spell attack roll against the target's AC, dealing 1d12 piercing damage on a hit with a tech target becomes glitching 2. On a critical hit, the target takes double damage, and a tech target becomes glitching 4.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d12.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 to 120 feet","tgt":"1 creature"},{"id":"optics-feed","n":"Optics Feed","fid":"FhcGSV1rbFWHiXJD","t":["concentrate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You tap into the optical scanners of a machine and turn it into a live camera feed. For the spell's duration, you can stream what the target sees via any screen you touch.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** The spell's duration is 1 hour.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The spell's duration is 1 day.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"overheat","n":"Overheat","fid":"wOjoJjl2ndZKTuFJ","t":["concentrate","fire","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You vent heat toward a nearby target. You deal 2d6 fire damage to the target. On a failed save, the target's held equipment becomes hot to the touch for the next round. Unless the target drops its currently held equipment at the start of its turn, it takes 3*rank fire damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6. Increase the damage of touching affected objects by 3.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"phantasmal-minion","n":"Phantasmal Minion","fid":"xqmHD8JIjak15lRk","t":["concentrate","manipulate","summon"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You summon a phantasmal minion. The minion is roughly the shape of a humanoid. You can choose to have it be Invisible or have an ephemeral appearance, but it's obviously a magical effect, not a real creature.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"60 feet","sus":1},{"id":"read-memory","n":"Read Memory","fid":"5ZG4T2nGy1g2RJvA","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You touch a computer screen, learning what it has recently displayed, even if it's been rebooted or used for something else since then. You choose one of the following pieces of information, and the computer truthfully displays or plays it.\n\n- The last command entered into the target.\n\n- The name of the last file accessed on the target.\n\n- The name of the last file downloaded to or uploaded from the target.\n\n- The last 1 minute of audio played from the target.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** Choose two of the options.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** Choose all of the options.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 functional comm unit or computer you can access"},{"id":"reparative-nanites","n":"Reparative Nanites","fid":"327oTvddhYQ012QG","t":["concentrate","healing","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You conjure a cloud of nanites that repair the target on a molecular level. The target gains fast healing 1.\n\nReparative Nanites\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The fast healing increases by 1.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"ricochet","n":"Ricochet","fid":"sXnWQOcGG2ELcxXb","t":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate","metal"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"A spinning disk or smooth orb of shimmering steel leaps from one target to another. You deal 2d4 bludgeoning or slashing damage (with a basic Reflex save).\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d4.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"cantrip","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 or 2 creatures","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"scrap-shell","n":"Scrap Shell","fid":"rBlHYUZH1anYD4cg","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"**Trigger** You're critically hit by a damage-dealing effect or Strike.\n\n---\n\nYou snap a layer of brittle scrap into place between you and the triggering blow, the scrap shatters and absorbs some of the force of the impact. The scrap has Hardness 5 and 10 healing Hit Points. If the scrap is destroyed, you take any excess damage that the scrap didn't absorb. After taking the blow, the scrap collapses into a pile of junk.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The scrap's Hit Points increase by 10.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"Reaction"},{"id":"scrap-spray","n":"Scrap Spray","fid":"dO7QnIrHTwmCzKQB","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You spray a blast of jagged scrap in an area in front of you. The scrap spray deals 1d6 bludgeoning, slashing, or piercing damage to each creature in the area. Each creature must attempt a Reflex save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Suppressed until the beginning of your next turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is suppressed until the beginning of your next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** Increase the damage by 3d6.","trad":[],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","area":"15-foot cone"},{"id":"shifting-surge","n":"Shifting Surge","fid":"7P4eBdqWcgQJAFCa","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You release a surge of magical energy that temporarily changes the type of damage dealt by a weapon. The next Strike the weapon makes deals your choice of acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage and deals an additional 1d6 extra damage of the same type as the weapon's normal damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The extra damage increases by 1d6.\n\nShifting Surge","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"one weapon held by you or a willing ally that deals acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage","dur":"1 minute or until discharged"},{"id":"sonic-scream","n":"Sonic Scream","fid":"QpP30fcEl4NGjHwo","t":["concentrate","manipulate","sonic"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You unleash a painfully rapid cone of vibrations by letting out a cathartic scream, dealing 1d8 sonic damage to creatures in the area with a basic Fortitude save. A creature that fails its saving throw also becomes Sickened 1.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Increases the damage by 1d8.","trad":["arcane","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"15-foot cone","save":"basic Fortitude"},{"id":"summon-robot","n":"Summon Robot","fid":"KlJEDmAOk1ztdNFf","t":["concentrate","manipulate","summon"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You summon a creature that has the tech trait and whose level is –1 to fight for you.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened** As listed in the summon trait.","trad":["arcane"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"30 feet","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"supercharge-weapon","n":"Supercharge Weapon","fid":"SbBqa1HStMrV47fb","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You draw in and condense ambient magical energy from around you to power up a weapon. The next Strike made using that weapon is supercharged. That Strike deals an additional 1d6 damage of the same type as the weapon's normal damage.\n\nSupercharge Weapon\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The extra damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 weapon held by you or a willing ally","dur":"1 minute or until discharged"},{"id":"wishborne-shot","n":"Wishborne Shot","fid":"NjsSsNlo2H0Duj7A","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"TC","d":"You wish for your next shot to go where you desire. The next time you make a Strike with the locus before the end of your turn, you ignore your target's cover and any flat check required due to the target being Concealed or hidden.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2"},{"id":"wisp-ally","n":"Wisp Ally","fid":"Sqo1uzSmebVWpqoT","t":["concentrate","light","manipulate"],"lv":1,"src":"PC","d":"You summon a Tiny bouncing wisp of light that easily distracts even the most determined of combatants. The wisp floats near your target. A wisp doesn't take up space, grant flanking, or have any other attributes a creature would. The wisp generates bright light in a 10-foot radius. When you Cast the Spell and each time you Sustain the spell, your wisp attempts to distract your target, which must succeed at a Will save or become Off-Guard until the start of your next turn. A creature who critically succeeds becomes immune to wisp ally for 1 hour.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** You create one additional wisp, allowing you to choose a different target. Each wisp you create must have a different target, and all of them attempt to distract their targets at the same time when you cast or Sustain this spell.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"one creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Will","sus":1},{"id":"build-bulkhead-stronghold","n":"Build Bulkhead Stronghold","fid":"fD644qK2ftpFhebf","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":10,"src":"TC","d":"You rapidly conjure a small technological stronghold that surrounds you, and all enemies are pushed to the nearest safe empty space outside of the area. The stronghold has AC 10, Hardness 10, and 150 healing Hit Points, and it's immune to critical hits and precision damage. It has the tech trait. Several large robotic legs sprout from the stronghold, allowing it to move with you, constantly keeping you at its center. The stronghold automatically opens to allow allies to enter while enemies are kept out. When you move in such a way that enemies would enter the area, they're instead pushed to the nearest safe empty space. Enemies can't enter the stronghold. Allies within the stronghold gain the benefits of standard cover, and all allies who start their turn within the stronghold gain 10 temporary Hit Points that last for the spell's duration.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","area":"10-foot emanation"},{"id":"event-horizon","n":"Event Horizon","fid":"0pl80qKToraH4dvO","t":["concentrate","manipulate","void"],"lv":10,"src":"PC","d":"You unleash the power of a supermassive black hole. All creatures in the area take 6d10 bludgeoning and 6d10 void damage. Event horizon ignores up to 10 resistance creatures in the area have to bludgeoning, and up to 10 resistance they have to void. Each creature attempts a Reflex save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and is Slowed 1 until the end of its next turn.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage, is Slowed 3 until the end of its next turn, and slowed 1 for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, is slowed 3 until the end of its next turn, and Slowed 2 for 1 minute.","trad":["primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"500 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"50-foot burst","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"new-game","n":"New Game","fid":"jon2tSGg7fSTqtk9","t":["concentrate","extradimensional","manipulate"],"lv":10,"src":"PC","d":"You draw creatures into a vidgame, digitizing their bodies and minds, including equipment, to play in virtual reality. The genre of the game and effect of the spell depend on who you target when you cast it. Any creature targeted by this spell becomes immune to it for 24 hours, no matter what genre they experience.\n\n- If you cast the spell targeting yourself and any number of willing allies, the targets enter a relaxing slice-of-life social simulation game where they can perform up to 1 hour of activities for the duration of the spell, including Refocusing, Repairing items, or simply evading an enemy by hiding in this virtual extradimensional space.\n- If you cast this spell targeting yourself or one willing ally, and one enemy, the targets enter a PvP game and are instructed to fight, using their current initiative. For the duration of the spell, either creature can manipulate fate once on each of its turns. This allows it to either roll twice and take the higher result on an attack roll or skill check it attempts against its opponent (a fortune effect) or force the opponent to roll twice on a saving throw against one of its abilities and take the lower result (a misfortune effect). The GM might decide that other genres of games exist that add additional rules or subsystems to resolving the spell. The spell ends if either target becomes unable to act or if they both agree to cease hostilities. Any results of the game, such as damage or conditions, persist after the game is over. If a player dies in this game, they die in real life.\n- If you cast this spell targeting one enemy, the target enters a PvE or puzzle game that traps them until they can complete the game. Once each turn, the target can spend 1 action to attempt a Computers or Perception check against your spell DC to escape the game. Teleportation magic doesn't help the creature escape unless the magic can transport someone into or out of a virtual space. When the spell ends, either because the target escaped or the duration ran out, the target returns to the space it occupied when it was digitized, or to the nearest space if the original is now filled. The GM might decide that other genres of games allow for different skill checks but should only do so if the target has proficiency in the listed skill.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target completes the game and the spell ends.\n\n**Success** The target makes progress toward completing the game. If the target already made progress, it completes the game and the spell ends.\n\n**Failure** The target makes no progress toward completing the game.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target loses the game and has to start over. It loses all progress it made.","trad":["arcane"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"varies","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"animal-form","n":"Animal Form","fid":"wp09USMB3GIW1qbp","t":["concentrate","manipulate","polymorph"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You call upon primal energy to transform yourself into a Medium animal battle form. When you Cast this Spell, choose a listed battle form. You can decide the specific type of animal (such as lion or snow leopard for cat), but this has no effect on the form's Size or statistics. While in this form, you gain the animal trait. You can Dismiss the spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which animal you choose:\n\n- AC = 16 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n- 5 temporary Hit Points.\n- Low-light vision and imprecise scent 30 feet.\n- One or more unarmed melee attacks specific to your battle form, which are the only attacks you can Strike with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +9, and your damage bonus is +1. These attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the Enfeebled condition, for example). If your unarmed attack bonus is higher, you can use it instead.\n- Athletics modifier of +9, unless your own modifier is higher.\n\n---\n\nYou also gain specific abilities based on the type of animal you choose:\n\n- **Ape**\n\nSpeed 25 feet, climb Speed 20 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ fist, **Damage** 2d6 bludgeoning.\n\n- **Bear**\n\nSpeed 30 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ jaws, **Damage** 2d8 piercing;\n- **Melee** ◆ claw (agile), **Damage** 1d8 slashing.\n\n- **Bull**\n\nSpeed 30 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ horn, **Damage** 2d8 piercing.\n\n- **Canine**\n\nSpeed 40 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ jaws, **Damage** 2d8 piercing.\n\n- **Cat**\n\nSpeed 40 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ jaws, **Damage** 2d6 piercing;\n- **Melee** ◆ claw (agile), **Damage** 1d10 slashing.\n\n- **Deer**\n\nSpeed 50 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ antler, **Damage** 2d6 piercing.\n\n- **Frog**\n\nSpeed 25 feet, swim Speed 25 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ jaws, **Damage** 2d6 bludgeoning;\n- **Melee** ◆ tongue (reach 15 feet), **Damage** 2d4 bludgeoning.\n\n- **Shark**\n\nswim Speed 35 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ jaws, **Damage** 2d8 piercing;\n- breathe underwater but not in air.\n\n- **Snake**\n\nSpeed 20 feet, climb Speed 20 feet, swim Speed 20 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ fangs, **Damage** 2d4 piercing plus 1d6 poison.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** You instead gain 10 temporary HP, AC = 17 + your level, attack modifier +14, damage bonus +5, and Athletics +14.\n\n**Heightened (4th)** Your battle form is Large and your attacks have 10-foot reach. You must have enough space to expand into or the spell is lost. You instead gain 15 temporary HP, AC = 18 + your level, attack modifier +16, damage bonus +9, and Athletics +16.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** Your battle form is Huge and your attacks have 15-foot reach. You must have enough space to expand into or the spell is lost. You instead gain 20 temporary HP, AC = 18 + your level, attack modifier +18, damage bonus +7 and double the number of damage dice, and Athletics +20.","trad":["primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"biomechanical-symbiosis","n":"Biomechanical Symbiosis","fid":"a8t4GpinUPJE0oLO","t":["concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"You redirect magical power through your target's circuitry, stimulating hybrid magical and technological healing. The target regains 2 Hit Points immediately and the first time each round for the duration of the spell. Whenever the target takes electricity damage or rolls a flat check due to the glitching condition, it also regains 2 Hit Points.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The Hit Points regained increase by 2.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature with the tech trait or with a tech augmentation","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"bolster-weapon","n":"Bolster Weapon","fid":"GdvESca5RRPKA2Ji","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"You use some of your magic to empower a weapon, creating an idealized version of the armament. When you cast this spell, choose one of the following traits: agile, backswing, forceful, reach, or sweep. The target weapon gains the chosen trait.\n\nBolster Weapon\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can target up to five weapons, choosing a trait for each weapon.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 powered melee weapon","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"caustic-conversion","n":"Caustic Conversion","fid":"GB1RVtoFPwyH1B9G","t":["acid","attack","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You launch a torrent of magical nanites that begin dissolving your target. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, you deal 3d8 acid damage plus 1d6 persistent acid damage. On a critical hit, double the initial damage, but not the persistent damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The initial damage increases by 2d8, and the persistent acid damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 creature"},{"id":"circuit-trace","n":"Circuit Trace","fid":"jqnRZasqIRUAP2Uy","t":["concentrate","manipulate","metal"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"A tangle of golden and copper threads fills the space around you and trails behind you, making it difficult for others to pass. When you Cast the Spell and the first time you Sustain it on each subsequent round, you Stride up to your Speed or 25 feet (whichever is lower), trailing wires behind you as the square you left becomes difficult terrain for the duration. You ignore difficult terrain created by circuit trace.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** The spell creates greater difficult terrain.","trad":["primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"conjure-junkrod","n":"Conjure Junkrod","fid":"iIub6uEavnMJEN4z","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"You configure a heap of scrap within range into a fully functioning vehicle. The junk becomes a level 0 land vehicle, such as a hoverboard, in an unoccupied adjacent space. The vehicle is clearly temporary, can't be sold or traded, and falls apart into worthless junk when the spell ends. The spell ends early if the vehicle becomes broken.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (3rd)** You create a 1st-level or lower land or water vehicle, such as a boatercycle or forklift.\n\n**Heightened (4th)** You create a 4th-level or lower land or water vehicle, such as an urban cruiser or torpedo minisub.\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You create a 5th-level or lower air, land, or water vehicle, such as a skyboat or turboglider.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** You create a 7th-level or lower vehicle of any kind, such as a drop pod.\n\n**Heightened (7th)** You create a 9th-level or lower vehicle.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** You create an 11th-level or lower vehicle.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** You create a 13th-level or lower vehicle.\n\n**Heightened (10th)** You create a 15th-level or lower vehicle.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"10 minutes","rng":"30 feet","dur":"8 hours"},{"id":"corrupt-machine","n":"Corrupt Machine","fid":"iE2Zih3Uyq87oHjH","t":["concentrate","manipulate","unholy"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"You fuse an unholy spirit into the target, causing it to morph into a visibly horrifying version. The weapon gains the unholy trait and deals an additional 1d4 fire damage on hit. Creatures critically hit by this weapon also become Frightened 1.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (4th)** The damage increases to 2d4.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The damage increases to 3d4.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** The damage increases to 4d4.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 tech weapon that’s unattended or wielded by a willing creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"deadly-vitality","n":"Deadly Vitality","fid":"J9IWyHhvdtMVBjqg","t":["concentrate","curse","death","manipulate","void"],"lv":2,"src":"Guilt of the Grave World","d":"You reach out across the strands of the universe and strangle the root of life that might flow into a living creature, cursing them to suffer for every bit of vitality they recover. If the target creature would receive any form of healing while under the effects of this spell, they afterward take damage from *deadly vitality*, potentially canceling out any healing they might have just received. This damage is dependent on the results of the creature's saving throw, made when the spell is first cast.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes an amount of void damage equal to half the amount of healing they just received (rounded down), to a maximum of 5 damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes an amount of void damage equal to the amount of healing they just received, to a maximum of 10 damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creatures takes an amount of void damage equal to the amount of healing they just received, to a maximum of 20 damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** Increase the amount of damage dealt by this spell's success condition by 5, its failure condition by 10, and its critical failure condition by 20.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 living creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"detect-thoughts","n":"Detect Thoughts","fid":"qOLMHvkAGsVYLhtn","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You sense the presence of thinking creatures around you. You detect the presence or absence of thoughts from conscious creatures that have Intelligence modifiers of –3 or higher. You can choose to ignore the thoughts of creatures you're familiar with so they don't interfere with your detection of other thoughts. The spell can penetrate some barriers, but 3 feet of dirt or wood, 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of metal, a thin sheet of lead, or any force barrier blocks it. Creatures who are immune to mental effects are immune to detection by this spell.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (4th)** You detect the number of thinking minds and whether or not the creatures are telepathic. Creatures with telepathy have louder thoughts than creatures who don't have telepathy and might be able to sense your intrusion, at the GM's discretion.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"30-foot emanation"},{"id":"doom-scroll","n":"Doom Scroll","fid":"VIKDSgBRR3Wd1mQx","t":["concentrate","incapacitation","manipulate","visual"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You magically broadcast grim news onto nearby devices, holo projectors, screens, and other displays (including comm units on armor). Creatures in the area who can see one or more displays must attempt a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Fascinated by the display.\n\n**Failure** The creature is fascinated by the display and Frightened 2 (even if the fascination ends).\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is fascinated by the display, Frightened 3, and Doomed 1 (even if the fascination ends).","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"15-foot burst","save":"Will","sus":1},{"id":"emoji-shield","n":"Emoji Shield","fid":"ONyatkj2Ds1laXLO","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"You create a shield emoji that protects you from harm and explodes in a burst of blinding light when it's broken into magical code. You gain a +1 status bonus to AC and the Emoji Burst reaction.\n\nEmoji Shield","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute or until dismissed","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"everlight","n":"Everlight","fid":"ynm8JIU3sc3qUMpa","t":["concentrate","light","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"The gemstone you touch glows, spreading bright light with a color of your choice in a 20-foot radius (and dim light for the next 20 feet). The spell ends immediately if the gemstone is broken.\n\nEverlight","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"touch","tgt":"a gemstone worth 60 credits or more","dur":"unlimited"},{"id":"inject-nanobots","n":"Inject Nanobots","fid":"ZofLZ5Zs8NN5yDPJ","t":["acid","attack","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You inject magical nanobots into a creature. Make a melee spell attack roll. On a hit, the target takes 4d6 acid damage. On a critical hit, the target takes double damage and becomes Confused for 1 round as nanobots swarm through the target's biological or mechanical systems.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":["arcane"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature"},{"id":"instant-virus","n":"Instant Virus","fid":"mnoTqz0gjRmuc4oR","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"Your touch installs a dangerous self-replicating virus that disrupts a technological creature's programming. The target must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is Glitching 1.\n\n**Failure** The target is glitching 1 and Stunned 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is Glitching 2 and Stunned 2.","trad":["arcane"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature with the tech trait","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"liquid-siphon","n":"Liquid Siphon","fid":"j6KI3dFuaYJmMSZh","t":["concentrate","manipulate","water"],"lv":2,"src":"Guilt of the Grave World","d":"You drain the moisture out of your target, crumpling them up like an empty beverage can and potentially leaving them a desiccated husk of what they once were. A nonliving target with liquid in its body (such as a vampire, water elemental, or keg of alcohol) can be affected by this spell, but a living creature with no vital liquids is immune. The target creature takes 4d6 bludgeoning damage, depending on the results of its saving throw.\n\nA target that fails its saving throw creates water that flows into your hands or a held container (1 gallon for Tiny, 2 gallons for Small, 4 for Medium, 6 for Large, 8 for Huge). If the target critically fails its saving throw, double this amount.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is Drained 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but double damage and the target is Drained 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Increase the damage by 2d6.","trad":["arcane","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature or object (see text)","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"logic-bomb","n":"Logic Bomb","fid":"ijlB3l9IBnpppfK0","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You implant a hazard containing a mind-blowing amount of information into the target. The hazard has a Stealth and Disable DC equal to your spell DC and requires one successful Computers check to disable. The first time a creature unsuccessfully attempts to access, destroy, or otherwise manipulate the target (such as using the Computers skill, failing to hit with a Strike, or otherwise), logic bomb detonates, and the creature takes 6d6 mental damage with a basic Will save. The spell ends when it's triggered or the duration ends, whichever comes first.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 computer or item with the tech trait","dur":"until the next time you make your daily preparations","save":"basic Will"},{"id":"optic-blast","n":"Optic Blast","fid":"H1DWnlnm2DupjAep","t":["concentrate","force","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"Your eyes boil with magical energy, building up pressure behind the locus until it bursts forth. Creatures in the area take 3d6 force damage with a basic Reflex save. Creatures that fail their save are also knocked back 5 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"30-foot line","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"peaceful-rest","n":"Peaceful Rest","fid":"xRgU9rrhmGAgG4Rc","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"The targeted corpse doesn't decay, nor can it be transformed into an undead. If the corpse is subject to a spell that requires the corpse to have died within a certain amount of time (for example, Raise Dead), do not count the duration of *peaceful rest* against that time. This spell also prevents ordinary bugs and pests (such as maggots) from consuming the body.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** The spell's duration is unlimited, but the spell takes one more action to cast and requires a cost (embalming fluid worth 60 credits).","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 corpse","dur":"until the next time you make your daily preparations"},{"id":"robo-fist","n":"Robo-Fist","fid":"DwAvbUFR5LID5ebL","t":["concentrate","manipulate","morph"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"With a flash of magic, two of your limbs grow wires and plating before snapping together into a robotic structure, ending in an oversized and empowered robot fist. While you maintain these robot fists, the damage die for your fist increases to 1d6 instead of 1d4. You don't take the normal –2 circumstance penalty when making a lethal attack with your fist or any other unarmed attacks\n\nUp to twice when you Sustain this spell, you can launch one of your robot fists as a rocket, dealing 2d6 fire damage to all creatures in a 10-foot burst up to 60 feet away (basic Reflex save). Once you've launched both your robot fists, the spell ends.\n\nRobo-Fist\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The fire damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"1","rng":"60 feet","dur":"1 minute","save":"basic Reflex","sus":1},{"id":"sift-the-sphere","n":"Sift the Sphere","fid":"tVTJS07cKDA5rNgc","t":["concentrate","manipulate","prediction"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You ritually sift through the local infosphere and gain mystical insight about a topic. During the casting of this spell, ask about the results of a particular course of action. The spell can predict results up to 30 minutes into the future and reveals the GM's best guess among the following outcomes.\n\n- **Weal** The results will be good.\n- **Woe** The results will be bad.\n- **Weal and Woe** The results will be a mix of good and bad.\n- **Nothing** There won't be particularly good or bad results. The GM rolls a secret DC 6 flat check. On a failure, the result is always \"nothing.\" This makes it impossible to tell whether a \"nothing\" result is accurate. If anyone asks about the same topic as the first casting of sift the sphere during an additional casting, the GM uses the secret roll result from the first casting. If circumstances change, it's possible to get a different result.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (4th)** The spell can predict results up to 1 week into the future.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"10 minutes"},{"id":"skim-data","n":"Skim Data","fid":"v2S6tlilNbA4uGdM","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You touch one object and concentrate on a dataset contained within it, such as a story, message, file, infosphere site, audio recording, or video. You understand the gist of the dataset and can quickly locate the most relevant pages or sections to your search. If the dataset is written or otherwise communicated in a language you don't know, or you attempt to gain information from a computer you don't have access to (such as one with a password you don't know), the spell fails.\n\nIf you Cast this Spell as part of a Research activity, you treat a critical failure as a failure instead.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"one dataset contained within a touched object"},{"id":"soul-surge","n":"Soul Surge","fid":"HPHr5aoLMH4eVwaw","t":["attack","concentrate","manipulate","sanctified","spirit"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You channel your life force into a spear of energy. You lose 6 Hit Points or, if you're in a bond with a vitality network that has at least 12 Hit Points, you can reduce the vitality bond's Hit Points by 12 instead. Make a ranged spell attack against the target's AC. On a hit, you deal 6d6 spirit damage. On a critical hit, the target takes double damage and becomes Drained 1.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Increase the damage dealt by 2d6 and the Hit Points lost by 2 (or by 4 if you spend Hit Points from a vitality network).","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature"},{"id":"sure-tracking","n":"Sure Tracking","fid":"UeodgQQ4yBFDOPEK","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"TC","d":"You upgrade a weapon to fire ammunition that can make precise adjustments to its position in space to better track targets. A creature using the weapon reduces the penalty for firing into the weapon's second range increment from –2 to 0. Additionally, whenever a creature makes a ranged Strike with the weapon that targets a single creature, the attack ignores the target's circumstance bonus to AC from cover.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can target up to 10 weapons.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 ranged weapon with the tech trait","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"temporal-bullets","n":"Temporal Bullets","fid":"H0WECXb2wvTHT9yk","t":["concentrate","fortune","manipulate"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"**Trigger** You fail (but not critically fail) an attack roll with a weapon.\n\n---\n\nYou rewind time and adjust probability to ensure an attack that just missed still does damage to its intended target. Roll damage as though you hit the target with the Strike, but the target only takes half the damage. You are then immune to temporal bullets for 10 minutes.","trad":["occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"reaction"},{"id":"twisted-vision","n":"Twisted Vision","fid":"XhypWjpV3NP76ahy","t":["concentrate","illusion","manipulate","mental","visual"],"lv":2,"src":"Guilt of the Grave World","d":"You blur a creature's senses, preventing them from recognizing their own allies in the heat of battle. This spell was developed by the Corpse Fleet to target living mystics and envoys who might heal or coordinate the actions of living enemies standing against their dread fleets. How badly this debilitates the target depends on the result of its saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Dazzled until the end of its next turn, but only for purposes of targeting their allies with beneficial effects or abilities.\n\n**Failure** The creature treats all of its allies as though they were undetected for purposes of targeting their allies with beneficial effects, abilities, or tactical movement. If the creature succeeds at the Seek action against this spell's save DC, they can treat their allies as hidden for the duration of the spell.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the creature cannot attempt to use the Seek action to find their allies while this spell is sustained.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Will","sus":1},{"id":"verdant-code","n":"Verdant Code","fid":"hk2mTLH9DIvNqDuS","t":["concentrate","manipulate","plant","wood"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You cause flowering vines or other plant matter to grow from an unattended tech object. Plant matter explodes from the target object, filling all squares within a 20-foot burst. Whenever a creature starts its turn in the area, it takes 2d6 piercing damage (basic Reflex save). On a critical failure, the creature is Immobilized for 1 round or until it Escapes against your spell DC. The growth covers the object, requiring a creature to succeed at a DC 5 flat check to physically access the object for the spell's duration.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 unattended object with the tech trait","area":"20-foot burst","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"vibe-check","n":"Vibe Check","fid":"wRNRWwCEbmSxbHDl","t":["concentrate","emotion","manipulate","mental"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You share a mood by psychically projecting an intense emotion into a creature's mind. The target attempts a Will save. On a failure, the target experiences your choice of the following emotions, but if you pick anger or joy this spell gains the incapacitation trait.\n\n- **Anger** On its next turn, the target spends its first action to attack the nearest creature, even if it's an ally.\n- **Joy** The target can't take any hostile actions.\n- **Fear** The target becomes Frightened 2.\n- **Sorrow** The target is Slowed 1 and bursts into tears.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (4th)** The spell affects all creatures in a 20-foot burst. Each creature must be affected by the same emotion.","trad":["occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 round","save":"Will"},{"id":"void-seed","n":"Void Seed","fid":"FIW0VpGULprL2u8J","t":["manipulate","void"],"lv":2,"src":"PC","d":"You plant a seed of entropy within a creature. The target gains the void healing ability. If the target would be healed by a non-void effect with the healing trait, it takes damage instead. An unwilling target can attempt a Will save to negate the effects.\n\nVoid Seed\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can target up to six living creatures.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 living creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Will"},{"id":"angelic-signal","n":"Angelic Signal","fid":"ftPpuRM57GD3SDBQ","t":["concentrate"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"**Trigger** An ally is targeted by an attack from a tech creature or a creature wielding a weapon with the tech trait.\n\n---\n\nAn angelic messenger swarms the attacking creature with nonsensical data derived from prayers emanating from their tech devices. The target must attempt a Will saving throw. Regardless of the result, the target becomes immune to angelic signal for 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes a –1 status penalty to all attack and damage rolls with tech weapons until the end of the turn.\n\n**Failure** The target takes a –2 status penalty to all attack and damage rolls with tech weapons until the end of the turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes a –3 status penalty to all attack and damage rolls with tech weapons until the end of the turn.\n\nAngelic Signal","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"reaction","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"the triggering creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"build-healing-station","n":"Build Healing Station","fid":"yG9AUj9Krcrx7U87","t":["concentrate","healing","manipulate","vitality"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You deploy a station in an adjacent empty space that floats in the air, fueling combatants and keeping them ready to fight on. The station is Small, visibly the source of the healing, has AC 10 and 30 Hit Points, and is immune to critical hits and precision damage. The station also has the tech trait. Anytime you or an ally ends a turn adjacent to the healing station, the adjacent character heals for 5 Hit Points and gains a +1 status bonus to saving throws for 1 round.\n\nBuild Healing Station\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+3)** The station's Hit Points increase by 30, and the healing increases by 5.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"build-sentries","n":"Build Sentries","fid":"tlGugw7XE5xYUsxZ","t":["concentrate","fire","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You deploy sentry turrets to attack intruders. For each action you spend Casting the Spell, you deploy a sentry turret into an empty space within range, attaching itself to any solid surface. These sentry turrets are Small and visibly dangerous. They have AC 10, Hardness 3, and 15 Hit Points and are immune to critical hits and precision damage. The sentries also have the tech trait. Whenever a visible creature that isn't Avoiding Notice, Hiding, or Sneaking comes within 15 feet of a sentry turret, you receive a ping and a small video feed of the creature on your comm unit. Once per round on subsequent turns, you can Interact with your comm unit to Command any number of sentry turrets to each fire a beam of energy at a creature within 30 feet of the sentry turret, dealing 2d6 fire damage (basic Reflex save). A creature can only be targeted by a single sentry turret each turn, even if it's within range of multiple sentries.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The Hit Points of each sentry turret increase by 10, and the damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"1 to 3","dur":"1 hour","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"censormoji","n":"Censormoji","fid":"kmhaxRaiLMJM6DOg","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"**Trigger** A creature within range Casts a Spell or performs an action with the auditory trait. You interrupt a creature's speech with a censoring emoji resembling a speaker with a line through it or a giant red X around its mouth or speakers. The triggering creature must attempt a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is Off-Guard until the end of your next turn.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Stupefied 1 and off-guard for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is Stupefied 3 and off-guard for 1 minute.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"reaction","rng":"15 feet","tgt":"the triggering creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"cozy-crashpad","n":"Cozy Crashpad","fid":"ASOR3qVrjqStL4Ph","t":["concentrate","exploration","manipulate","metal"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You shape a shack 20 feet on each side and 10 feet high. This shack has the structure trait and the same restrictions as magic items that create structures. The walls of the cottage are simple and metal, with small, metal shuttered windows, and it has one metal door. It doesn't include its own lock, but it has a fastener to which a lock can be applied.\n\nThe interior contains three cots, one toilet, and a small stove powered by magic. The interior is lit with a small magical light that you can light or extinguish at will using a Sustain action. The climate inside the shack is comfortable and allows creatures inside it to withstand most hostile weather conditions, but incredible heat or cold, powerful storms, and winds of hurricane force or greater destroy the cottage. Other creatures can freely enter and exit the shack without damaging it, but if you exit the shack, the spell ends. You can Dismiss the spell.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"1 minute","rng":"30 feet","dur":"12 hours"},{"id":"dancemoji","n":"Dancemoji","fid":"e98MfMLWgbwOFCZo","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You create a dancer emoji that inspires all that follow in its footsteps. When you Cast the Spell and the first time you Sustain it on each subsequent turn, the dancer emoji Flies or Strides up to 20 feet, leaving a trail of glowing dance floor in each space it travels through that lingers for the duration. Allies who enter the trail or start their turn there gain a +5-foot status bonus to their Speeds until the end of the turn. An ally who starts to Fly or Stride on the trail and doesn't leave it for the entire movement also gains a +1 circumstance bonus to their AC until the start of their next turn, mimicking the dancer's graceful movements.\n\nDancemoji (Speed Bonus)\n\nDancemoji (AC Bonus)","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"discharge","n":"Discharge","fid":"rBh2PjtbDGAjbcu6","t":["concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You ignite a sudden spark of electricity that surges into a technological creature or object. You de-energize an item with the tech trait or disrupt a creature with the tech trait, with effects based on the target being a creature or object.\n\n- **Creature** If your target is a creature with the tech trait, it attempts a Will save. On a failure, the creature is Glitching 1; on a critical failure, the creature is Glitching 2.\n- **Object** If you target an attended object, the creature with the object attempts a Will save. On a success, the object loses half of its maximum charges. On a failure, or if you target an unattended object, the object loses all its remaining charges.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature or object with the tech trait","save":"Will"},{"id":"electrotether","n":"Electrotether","fid":"Cbj7tDkb2ZTp10Cg","t":["attack","concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You supercharge the targets' electromagnetism and pull them with a tether of lightning. Make a ranged spell attack against each target. If you attack two targets, both attacks count toward your multiple attack penalty, but it doesn't increase until after both attacks. The targets each take 4d8 electricity damage and are pulled 5 feet closer to you, or 10 feet closer on a critical hit. If both attacks hit, you can choose to move the creatures closer to one another instead of closer to you. Moving a target into a barrier, creature, or obstacle causes the target to stop before entering that space.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d8.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"up to two creatures"},{"id":"emoji-armament","n":"Emoji Armament","fid":"QnVLetx8Ajiu5XVk","t":["concentrate","force","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You conjure an emoji of a weapon. Attempt a spell attack roll against a target's AC within 60 feet of the emoji (or adjacent if the emoji is a melee weapon), dealing 4d6 force damage on a hit (double damage on a critical hit). You can repeat the attack as a reaction when a creature in range uses a manipulate action (or move action, if the emoji is a melee weapon), but the spell ends at the start of your turn if you haven't used this reaction since the end of your previous turn. You can move the emoji each time you Sustain the Spell.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"entropy-strike","n":"Entropy Strike","fid":"kR5A0h2a9hY41wav","t":["acid","attack","concentrate","manipulate","void"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You unleash a ray of entropy that rapidly and indiscriminately decays matter. Make a ranged spell attack against the target's AC. On a hit, the target takes 5d8 void damage, or it takes 2d6 persistent acid damage and is glitching 1 if it has the tech trait. On a critical hit, double the damage, and if the creature has the tech trait, it's glitching 2 and Stunned 1.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1 die.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature or unattended object"},{"id":"feline-senses","n":"Feline Senses","fid":"1lv6Zmp2eWRIPn1n","t":["concentrate","manipulate","morph"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"Your senses improve as you gain feline eyes, ears, and whiskers. You gain darkvision and electromagnetic scent as an imprecise sense out to 30 feet, allowing you to detect living and technological creatures.\n\nFeline Senses\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (4th)** The spell's range is touch and it targets 1 willing creature.\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The spell's range is touch and it targets 1 willing creature. The duration is until your next daily preparations.\n\nFeline Senses (6th-Rank)","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 hour"},{"id":"ghost-killer-weapon","n":"Ghost Killer Weapon","fid":"c3pohoiOH2qIhDDp","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"The target weapon becomes translucent and ghostly, and it can affect material and incorporeal creatures and objects. It gains the effects of the ghost killer weapon upgrade, meaning it becomes magical if it wasn't already, is especially effective against incorporeal creatures, and can be wielded by a corporeal or incorporeal creature.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 weapon that's either unattended or wielded by you or a willing ally","dur":"5 minutes"},{"id":"holographic-memory","n":"Holographic Memory","fid":"eHiWtMiXoI1d48A7","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"r":"u","lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You reach into the target's mind, extract a specific memory you have some awareness of, and project it into a hologram. Alternatively, when casting this spell, you can choose to pull a random memory left to the GM's discretion. The holographic memory can be no longer than 5 minutes; if the extracted memory is longer than this, the hologram simply ends at that point. The hologram includes audio as well as visual components, but it doesn't contain haptic, olfactory, or other components. The hologram typically plays a memory that takes place in a single scene, though it can cut to multiple scenes if they're accurate to the memory and its length allows. The hologram plays the memory exactly as the target experienced it and from the target's perspective, so it often lacks context.\n\nThis spell can target any living, Unconscious, or deceased sentient creature with an Intelligence modifier of –3 or higher. If the target is deceased, it can't have been dead for longer than 1 week, or this spell fails; once a corpse has been subjected to holographic memory by any caster, any subsequent castings of holographic memory fail.\n\nIf the target is unwilling to share this memory, it can attempt a Will save to resist this spell.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature or corpse","save":"Will"},{"id":"hot-swap","n":"Hot Swap","fid":"32rKBaTBCJ33qixz","t":["concentrate","manipulate","teleportation"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You create a mystical bond between the targets, allowing them to switch positions. For the duration, creatures wielding either weapon gain the Swap action.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"touch","tgt":"2 unattended weapons","dur":"1 hour"},{"id":"infuse-ammo","n":"Infuse Ammo","fid":"0Ut3WWGJP2dpjSwY","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You enhance your next round of ammunition with the might of the elements, empowering the next round in the chamber. When you cast this spell, choose an elemental trait and corresponding type of damage: electricity or sonic for air, bludgeoning or piercing for earth, acid or slashing for metal, fire for fire, bludgeoning or cold for water, or piercing or poison for wood. The next Strike you make with the wielded weapon before the end of your next turn gains the chosen elemental trait, damage trait, and deals an additional 1d6 damage of the chosen type of damage.\n\nInfuse Ammo\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The additional damage increases to 2d6.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2"},{"id":"instant-messaging","n":"Instant Messaging","fid":"0P9ragdbl7dIH7aH","t":["concentrate","linguistic","manipulate","mental","visual"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You use your comm unit as a focus for communication, projecting messages to those nearby. You can communicate telepathically with creatures within 30 feet by using a free hand to type a message into your comm unit or whispering into the mic. This communication is one-way, and you can only communicate with creatures that share a language with you. You can choose which creatures receive your communications, and those creatures know you were the one who transmitted the message.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can communicate with images rather than words. *Instant messaging* loses the linguistic trait.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"irradiate","n":"Irradiate","fid":"MfsxPjshwZJZuNpN","t":["concentrate","manipulate","radiation"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You rapidly destabilize and decay the atoms around you to create a burst of magically enhanced mild radiation. Creatures in the area must attempt a Fortitude save against mild radiation sickness. This magical radiation uses your spell DC in place of the radiation's normal Fortitude DC, has an immediate onset, and the interval between each stage is 1 round. Technology doesn't gain the glitching condition from the radiation created by this spell.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** The radiation increases to severe.\n\n**Heightened (7th)** The radiation increases to extreme.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The radiation increases to incredible.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 hour","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"life-seal","n":"Life Seal","fid":"ShwUELLERVMtdjwE","t":["concentrate"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"**Trigger** A creature within range enters an environment that would be harmful to it.\n\nA shimmering bubble envelops the target's body, allowing it to breathe normally in a vacuum or other unsafe environment and protecting it from severe temperatures and radiation.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (7th)** You can target up to 5 additional creatures to gain protection against the environment the triggering creature entered. The spell lasts for 8 hours and also protects against extreme temperatures and radiation.\n\n**Heightened (10th)** You can target up to 10 additional creatures to gain protection against the environment the triggering creature entered. The spell lasts until your next daily preparations and also protects against incredible temperatures and radiation.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"reaction","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"the triggering creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"one-with-junk","n":"One with Junk","fid":"HT4nqVPlQKKi2jdV","t":["concentrate","manipulate","polymorph"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You can either transform into junk or merge with it. This spell has the same effects as One with Plants but lets you merge with or turn into a pile of junk or a larger piece of junk, such as trash bags, a heap of scrap metal, or a broken construct. Junk you turn into has AC 23. You can Dismiss this spell.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"10 minutes or 8 hours"},{"id":"personal-gravity","n":"Personal Gravity","fid":"0mNmVi9CLXor3McX","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You alter gravity's effects on you. You treat gravity as if it were your choice of one step higher or lower (for example, if you were in an area of low gravity, you could choose either standard gravity or zero-g). While the spell is active, you reduce the distance of any forced movement that would affect you by 5 feet (minimum 0 feet), and you ignore being clumsy and untethered because of gravity effects on you. You can Dismiss the spell.","trad":["arcane","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 hour"},{"id":"positronic-helmet","n":"Positronic Helmet","fid":"AZUxwGaKz3qTCMvk","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental","morph"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"A magical robotic headpiece builds out from you, transforming your brain into a central processing unit and bolstering your mind. You gain the tech trait for the duration of the spell. You gain a +1 status bonus to Perception checks and Will saves. You can Sustain this spell once per turn to fire a mental beam from the helmet that deals 2d10 mental damage to creatures in a 30-foot line with a basic Will save.\n\nPositronic Helmet\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d10.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","area":"30-foot line","save":"basic Will"},{"id":"selective-invisibility","n":"Selective Invisibility","fid":"L6Gww2b2YVM3q0ZQ","t":["illusion","manipulate","subtle"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"A willing creature you touch becomes Invisible to everyone except a second target within the spell's range. If the invisible creature uses a hostile action against anyone who isn't the target that can see them, the spell ends after that hostile action is completed.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** You can make up to 6 willing creatures within 30 feet invisible, but they all must have the same target.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"500 feet","tgt":"1 willing creature touched and one within range","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"share-pain","n":"Share Pain","fid":"EhN3GjdjXChMdiFk","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You telepathically share the sensation of agonizing pain with a creature. The target takes 3d12 mental damage and attempts a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Clumsy 1 for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Clumsy 2 for 1 minute.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The spell targets up to four creatures and deals 6d12 mental damage.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"skyfire-wings","n":"Skyfire Wings","fid":"VmtQlZqeraTv0Eer","t":["concentrate","electricity","fire","manipulate","morph"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"Wings of plasma grow from your body that propel you to soar high above your enemies, or scorch them for getting too close. You gain a fly Speed equal to your Speed or 20 feet, whichever is greater. Your arms (or primary set of arms) turn into wings that can't hold items or wield weapons. You drop any held equipment in those arms. You gain a wing unarmed attack that deals 1d8 fire damage and has the backswing, reach, and unarmed traits. On a critical hit, a target of your wing attack takes 2 persistent electricity damage.\n\nSkyfire Wings (3rd-Rank)\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** Your wings deal 2d8 fire damage and 4 persistent electricity damage on a critical hit. The duration increases to 5 minutes.\n\nSkyfire Wings (5th-Rank)\n\n**Heightened (7th)** Your wings deal 3d8 fire damage and 6 persistent electricity damage on a critical hit. The duration increases to 1 hour.\n\nSkyfire Wings (7th-Rank)\n\n**Heightened (9th)** Your wings deal 4d8 fire damage and 8 persistent electricity damage on a critical hit. The duration increases to 8 hours.\n\nSkyfire Wings (9th-Rank)","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"times-edge","n":"Time's Edge","fid":"GdlG9a4o0ax0F2HT","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"You refract latent energy from the Dimension of Time into your current plane in the form of a massive blade. The blade deals 5d6 slashing damage to all creatures in the area as it causes time to pass rapidly in a thin slice of their bodies. Creatures in the area must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Sickened 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is Sickened 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":["occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"60-foot line","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"turbulent-toys","n":"Turbulent Toys","fid":"jAPEfvqa62jUPuL6","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"Magical battery-powered children's toys fill the area and begin rolling, bumping, and flipping over one another. The toys are semi-corporeal constructs that can't be moved or damaged. When you Cast the Spell and the first time you Sustain it each subsequent round, you choose the turbulence the toys create, then move the area up to 5 feet.\n\n- **Ankle Bumpers** The toys jostle against the feet of creatures in the area, and each creature must succeed at a Reflex save or fall Prone.\n\n- **Battery Hogs** The toys steal energy to power themselves. All battery-operated devices in the area lose 2 charges.\n\n- **Strobe Rave** The toys unleash a dizzying array of flashing lights and puffs of colored smoke. Each creature in the area must succeed at a Will save or be Dazzled until the start of your next turn. This effect has the visual trait.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"10-foot burst","sus":1},{"id":"upgrade-construct","n":"Upgrade Construct","fid":"nMOmER5WBdCEkn6v","t":["concentrate","manipulate","morph"],"lv":3,"src":"TC","d":"You upgrade the weapons and armor of the target. The target gains a +1 status bonus to AC, and the target's Strikes deal an additional 2d4 damage of the same type as the base weapon.\n\nUpgrade Construct\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+3)** The status bonus to AC increases by 1, and the additional damage increases by 1d4.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature with the tech trait","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"void-whispers","n":"Void Whispers","fid":"qkehzRdn7JeGrR6E","t":["auditory","concentrate","incapacitation","linguistic","manipulate","mental"],"lv":3,"src":"PC","d":"The target hears ominous sounds containing unspeakable mysteries from beyond the stars that disorient its mind. The target attempts a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target hears the strange whispers, becoming Stupefied 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target begins to wander aimlessly, using each action to Step in a random direction. When it moves, the target takes the safest route and doesn't enter hazardous terrain. The spell has a duration of 1 minute or until a creature uses a hostile action against the target.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, except the target babbles incoherently. Any creature that begins its turn within 20 feet of the target must attempt a Will saving throw. On a failure, it must use its first action on its next turn to Step in a random direction and becomes immune to this spell for 24 hours. This is an incapacitation effect.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"varies","save":"Will"},{"id":"animate-armor","n":"Animate Armor","fid":"aKWVS9cT4q22loRJ","t":["concentrate","manipulate","summon"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You imbue your armor with a fragment of your own will, causing the outer plating to fly off you and assist in the fight of its own accord. You summon an Animated Tech Armor to fight for you. The animated tech armor can use any abilities of the armor as if it were Activated and worn by it.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (5th)** The summoned armor has the aerial and elite adjustments.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"battle-sonata","n":"Battle Sonata","fid":"Fa1f7VtZitQYrArX","t":["concentrate","manipulate","sonic"],"lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"This spell was composed by pahtra battle singers of Pulonis to amplify a dissonant song into a deadly wave that deals 4d10 sonic damage. Each creature must attempt a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Deafened for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, is deafened for 1 minute, and becomes Stunned 1.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d10.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"15-foot cone","save":"Will"},{"id":"bombarding-emojis","n":"Bombarding Emojis","fid":"vuiUvfh3ptO9gnDI","t":["concentrate","force","manipulate"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You conjure a barrage of emojis that rain from the sky. Creatures in the area take 6d8 force damage (basic Reflex save). When you Cast the Spell and the first time you Sustain it each subsequent round, each creature in the area takes 6d8 force damage (basic Reflex save).","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"100 feet","area":"10-foot burst","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"build-booster-ring","n":"Build Booster Ring","fid":"yIRR3rgI0gtNrKQf","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You use magical tech to create a ring that's 1 inch thick, 10 feet wide, and 10 feet high. You must create the ring in an unbroken open space so its edges don't pass through any creatures or objects, or the spell is lost. The ring contains a ripple in space-time that amplifies those that pass through it. Creatures or vehicles that move through the ring gain a +30-foot status bonus to their Speeds until the end of the turn.\n\nBuild Booster Ring","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","dur":"1 round"},{"id":"build-shield-generator","n":"Build Shield Generator","fid":"q0JMsrMuk19oLzXY","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You bind together magic and science to create a shield generator in an empty adjacent space. The generator is Small, visibly the source of the shields, has AC 10 and 40 Hit Points, and is immune to critical hits and precision damage. The generator also has the tech trait. This generator provides a small, shimmering light that covers you and all allies within 60 feet, granting a +1 status bonus to AC, as well as resistance 4 to acid, cold, electricity, fire, force, and sonic damage. If the generator is destroyed, the spell ends.\n\nBuild Shield Generator\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The generator's Hit Points increase by 10, and the resistance granted by the generator increases by 1.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"burstmoji","n":"Burstmoji","fid":"pccdWdF0fwU3UKzZ","t":["concentrate","fire","manipulate"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You create an emoji of an explosion that erupts into a mass of flames. Creatures in the area take 6d6 fire damage (basic Reflex save), and the area becomes difficult and hazardous terrain for the duration. Creatures that start their turn in the area or move through a square in the area take (rank + (rank - 3)) fire damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The initial fire damage increases by 2d6, and the hazardous terrain fire damage increases by 2.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"200 feet","area":"20-foot burst","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"cable-management","n":"Cable Management","fid":"nam1metCZqYItFck","t":["concentrate","manipulate","metal"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"A massive tangle of interconnected computer cables springs forth from every direction at once. Spaces in the area become difficult terrain for the duration. Each time a creature begins a move action inside the tangle or enters the tangle during a move action, it must succeed at a Reflex save or take a –10-foot status penalty to its Speeds until it leaves the area. On a critical failure, the creature is also Immobilized for 1 round. In addition, the cables are so thickly tangled that they provide standard cover to creatures in the area.\n\nCable Management","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"5-foot burst","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"cairn-form","n":"Cairn Form","fid":"HAaRcHfN4g83eSEC","t":["concentrate","earth","manipulate","morph"],"lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"Your target's skin becomes a thick carapace of solid stone, granting resistance 5 to physical damage, except adamantine. The target gains a fist unarmed attack that deals 2d6 bludgeoning damage. The target uses their highest weapon or unarmed attack proficiency with these attacks, and if they have weapon specialization or greater weapon specialization, they add this damage as well. On a critical hit with one of these unarmed attacks, the creature struck must succeed at a Fortitude save against the target's class DC or become Stunned 1 for 1 round.\n\nCairn Form\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The resistance increases to 10, and the damage dealt by the attacks increases to 3d6.\n\n**Heightened (10th)** The resistance increases to 20, and the damage dealt by the attacks increases to 4d6.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"cosmic-radiation-rods","n":"Cosmic Radiation Rods","fid":"hMYeUxTRfjSDhSRL","t":["concentrate","manipulate","radiation"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You summon forth an intangible field of thousands of tiny control rods to absorb ambient radiation. These rods hover in the air all around you but are too small to affect sight lines or otherwise interfere with targeting. All allies within the area gain resistance 5 to damage from radiation effects and a +1 status bonus to Fortitude saves against poison and radiation effects.\n\nCosmic Radiation Rods\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+3)** The status bonus increases by 1, and the resistance increases by 5.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","area":"10-foot emanation","sus":1},{"id":"eldritch-wrath","n":"Eldritch Wrath","fid":"jyrxfWeeCsrkhNit","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You channel the bizarre powers that exist beyond the outer reaches of the universe, dealing 3d12 mental damage to each creature in the area as phantasmal claws, jaws, and tentacles lash out at each target. Each creature in the area must attempt a Will save. The area is difficult terrain for any creature sickened by the effects of this spell.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Sickened 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is Sickened 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d12.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","area":"20-foot burst","save":"Will"},{"id":"emoji-spam","n":"Emoji Spam","fid":"J0uCmkZq1uLAun94","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental","visual"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You overwhelm a creature's senses with a barrage of different emojis, each eliciting a different sensation, memory, or otherwise deeply rooted connection that causes their brain to overload with information. The creature takes 6d6 mental damage and must attempt a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and is Dazzled until the start of your next turn.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage plus an additional (item level - 3)d6 persistent mental damage. While taking this persistent damage, the creature is dazzled and can only speak in emojis. While speaking in only emojis, the creature can't cast spells or use auditory and sonic effects, except those that have \"emoji\" or \"moji\" in their name or the subtle trait. The creature can still communicate by speaking, but doing so loses the auditory trait and gains the visual trait.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the creature takes double damage, and the creature is Blinded while taking the persistent damage. When it loses the persistent damage, it becomes dazzled until the end of its next turn.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The mental damage increases by 2d6, and the persistent mental damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"explosion-of-rot","n":"Explosion of Rot","fid":"qAbHuohnFmiXx9sd","t":["concentrate","manipulate","poison"],"lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"A giant pustule swells and explodes, coating everything around it in life-draining rot. Creatures and plants in the area take 6d6 poison damage and must attempt a Reflex save. Foliage and plant matter in the area damaged by the spell no longer provide cover.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is Enfeebled 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes double damage, (floor((rank - 2)/2))d6 persistent poison damage, and is Enfeebled 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The initial damage increases by 2d6, and the persistent damage on a critical failure increases by 1d6.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","area":"20-foot burst","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"genetic-regeneration","n":"Genetic Regeneration","fid":"s6J1Q0e28Gb42epQ","t":["concentrate","healing","manipulate","vitality"],"lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You imbue the target's genetic code with a stimulating regenerative property that begins healing its wounds. The target temporarily gains regeneration 7, which restores 7 Hit Points to it at the start of each of its turns. While it has regeneration, the target can't die from taking damage, and its dying condition can't increase to a value that would kill it (this stops most creatures' dying condition at dying 3), though if its wounded value becomes 4 or higher, it stays Unconscious until its wounds are treated. If the target takes acid or fire damage, its regeneration deactivates until after the end of its next turn.\n\nOnce during the spell's duration, the creature can forgo healing Hit Points that round to regrow one damaged or ruined organ or reattach a severed body part by spending an Interact action to hold the body part to the area it was severed from.\n\nGenetic Regeneration\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Increase the regeneration value by 2.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 willing creature","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"ghostmoji","n":"Ghostmoji","fid":"5ndwZJL0Olg9gohU","t":["concentrate","emotion","fear","incapacitation","manipulate","mental"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You create a terrifying ghost emoji that only the target can see. The target must attempt a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is Frightened 1.\n\n**Failure** The target is Frightened 2 and Stunned 2.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is Frightened 3 and Fleeing, and it's Slowed 2 for as long as it remains frightened.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"holographic-stand-in","n":"Holographic Stand-In","fid":"4yllv8kIihHNb2xj","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You create a convincing holographic copy of yourself. This hologram looks exactly like you, but it's incorporeal and mimics your movements. When you Sustain the spell, you can Command the hologram to act differently. Characters can discern the nature of the hologram with a Perception check, or by interacting with it in any way, such as attempting to Strike it. You can look through the hologram's eyes by closing your own as part of a [[/act seek]] action. The spell immediately ends if you lose line of effect to your hologram.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The maximum duration you can Sustain the spell increases to 10 minutes.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"infectious-virus","n":"Infectious Virus","fid":"2Ln6XZujQYZK95Mv","t":["concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You craft a dangerous computer virus. All creatures with the tech trait in the area take 10 persistent electricity damage and must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage and is Glitching 1.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is Glitching 2.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes double damage and is Glitching 4.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The persistent damage increases by 5.","trad":["occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","area":"20-foot burst","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"light-shift","n":"Light Shift","fid":"Py97Kb5H6vrgELDa","t":["concentrate","light","manipulate","teleportation"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You fire the locus and instantly transfer yourself along the beam, transforming you and your equipment into photons for a fraction of a second. You teleport to an occupied space within the first range increment of the locus, and you shed bright light in a radius equal to the distance you teleported that lasts until the end of your turn.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2"},{"id":"speak-with-computers","n":"Speak with Computers","fid":"Nf6GqoHkNbfWJDQT","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You can ask questions of and receive answers from the spirits inhabiting a computer. These synthetic spirits manifest within computer code and often have personalities colored by the nature of the device, its condition, and its applications and personalized settings. A computer's perspective, perception, and knowledge give it a worldview different enough from a human's that it doesn't consider the same details important. Computers can mostly answer questions about creatures that interfaced with them in the past and what information is concealed within their files.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** The duration is 8 hours.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 hour"},{"id":"surveillance-vision","n":"Surveillance Vision","fid":"cn0QFZOBORN9mwr0","t":["concentrate","manipulate","scrying"],"lv":4,"src":"TC","d":"You create an invisible security camera with 1 HP and AC 10 anywhere within 10 feet on a solid surface. It sees in all directions with your normal visual senses. You can constantly perceive through your own senses and the vision of the camera as long as you're on the same plane. Only one camera can be active at a time; if you make a second camera, the first is destroyed. You can Dismiss this spell.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (7th)** The duration becomes unlimited.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"1 minute","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"1 solid surface","dur":"8 hours"},{"id":"weight-of-ages","n":"Weight of Ages","fid":"7Ib3qxIC0bFD3ued","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":4,"src":"PC","d":"You burden a creature's body and mind with the pains and sorrows of a lifetime. The target takes 3d8 bludgeoning damage and 3d8 mental damage and must attempt a Will saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is Encumbered for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes double damage and is encumbered for 1 minute.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The mental damage increases by 2d8.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Will"},{"id":"blinding-emoji","n":"Blinding Emoji","fid":"ZSlXevjqvcApnO36","t":["concentrate","light","manipulate","visual"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You create an emoji so bright that it wears sunshades to protect itself from its own light. Creatures in the area when you cast the spell or that start their turn in the area must attempt a Fortitude saving throw. When you Sustain the spell, you can move the area up to 30 feet.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected and temporarily immune to blinding emoji for 1 minute.\n\n**Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Failure** The creature is Blinded until the end of its next turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is blinded for 1 minute.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"20-foot burst","save":"Fortitude","sus":1},{"id":"carcinization","n":"Carcinization","fid":"n5a3t5Qnx5AU8auy","t":["incapacitation","manipulate","polymorph"],"lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You manipulate the target's genetic code and accelerate the inevitable, pressuring the target to undergo carcinization and become a crab. A willing target fully transforms into a crab, as if it had cast animal form heightened to the same rank as this spell and using the following statistics.\n\n- **Crab**\n\nSpeed 25 feet, swim 15 feet\n- **Melee** ◆ big claw, **Damage** 2d8 piercing\n- **Melee** ◆ claw (agile), **Damage** 2d4 piercing.\n- Can breathe air and water.\n\nCarcinization\n\nUnwilling targets must instead attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target's body gains minor features of a crab, its appendages turning into claws and causing it to become Clumsy 1.\n\n**Failure** The target transforms into a partial crab-like being, becoming clumsy 1, Stupefied 1, and Sickened 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target is transformed into a partial crab-like being and becomes Clumsy 2, Stupefied 2, and Sickened 2.","trad":["primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"chrono-push","n":"Chrono Push","fid":"g58dbrP7FadZhh6j","t":["attack","concentrate","force","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You push a creature across the battlefield so hard it slides through time. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, you knock the target back 15 feet in a straight line (30 feet on a critical hit). If the pushed creature makes contact with a solid barrier or another creature, its movement ends. At the end of this movement, the creature reenters the flow of time with a burst of temporal energy. The target and creatures now adjacent to the target take 7d8 force damage with a basic Reflex save.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The force damage increases by 1d8.","trad":["occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"500 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"control-machine","n":"Control Machine","fid":"7WtiWJRYZhT6a9Ey","t":["concentrate","incapacitation","manipulate"],"r":"u","lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You take control of a technological creature or object and command it telepathically. If you issue an obviously self-destructive order to a sapient target, the target doesn't act until you issue a new order. The effect depends on its Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target is Stunned 1 as it fights off your commands.\n\n**Failure** You control the target. It gains the controlled condition, but it can attempt a Will save at the end of each of its turns. On a success, the spell ends.\n\n**Critical Failure** As a failure, but the target receives a new save only if it's sapient and you give it a new order that's against its nature, such as killing its allies.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (10th)** The duration is unlimited.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature or hazard with the tech trait","dur":"until the next time you make your daily preparations","save":"Will"},{"id":"cosmic-eddy","n":"Cosmic Eddy","fid":"hY6HnTzr97uUqI2V","t":["concentrate","force","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You conjure a swirling eddy of magical force, battering your targets and hindering their movement. Creatures in the area when you Cast the Spell or that start their turn there take 6d6 force damage with a basic Reflex save; on a failure, a creature also falls Prone. The area is difficult terrain, and creatures attempting to Fly in the area must attempt an Acrobatics check against your spell DC; on a failure, the movement is disrupted, and any remaining movement from the action is wasted. In addition, unattended items of light Bulk or less are thrown around within the eddy and land in a random space in the area when the spell ends.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":["divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"divine-machine","n":"Divine Machine","fid":"TW5UKhYiXlT66Ivu","t":["concentrate","manipulate","polymorph"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You surround your target with shimmering divine magic that coalesces into technological armor, building them a large, resilient shell. For the duration of the spell, the target stands taller, functions more reliably, and gains supernatural protection from harm. The target grows to Large size unless it's already Large or larger. Its equipment grows with it but returns to its usual size if removed. Its reach increases by 5 feet (or by 10 feet if it started out Tiny). The target also gains a +2 status bonus to AC and saving throws and 20 temporary Hit Points for the duration. The spell ends immediately when the target has no temporary Hit Points.\n\nDivine Machine\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The temporary Hit Points granted by this spell increase by 5.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 ally with the tech trait","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"illusory-scene","n":"Illusory Scene","fid":"Ucf8eynbZMfUucjE","t":["auditory","concentrate","illusion","manipulate","olfactory","visual"],"lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You craft an imaginary scene that includes up to 10 discrete creatures or objects of various sizes, all of which must be within the spell's area. These elements generate appropriate sounds and smells, and they feel right to the touch. Elements of an illusory scene are incapable of speech. Unlike with the Illusory Creature spell, creatures in your scene lack combat abilities and statistics. Your scene doesn't include changes to the environment around it, though you can place your scene within the illusory environment of other illusion spells.\n\nWhen you create the scene, you can choose to have it be static or follow a program. Though a static scene is stationary, it includes basic natural movement. For example, wind blowing on an illusory piece of paper would rustle it. A program can be up to 1 minute long and repeats when finished. For instance, you could create a scene of two orcs fighting each other, and the fight would go the same way for each repetition. If you create a loop, the two fighters end up in the same place at the start of the scene and at the end of it, but you can smooth the program so it's hard to tell when the loop ends and begins. Anyone observing the scene for more than a few minutes almost always notices it looping. You're unable to alter the program after you create the illusion.\n\nAny creature that touches any part of the image or uses the Seek action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion. If they interact with a portion of the illusion, they disbelieve only that portion. They disbelieve the entire scene only on a critical success.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** Creatures or objects in your scene can speak. You must speak the specific lines for each actor when creating your program. The spell disguises your voice for each actor.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** As the 6th-rank version, and the duration is unlimited.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"10 minutes","rng":"500 feet","dur":"1 hour","area":"30-foot burst"},{"id":"overload-systems","n":"Overload Systems","fid":"5cMDrC3jX1yrxOzh","t":["concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You flood the area with a wave of electrical interference. You deal 7d8 electricity damage to creatures in the area. Each creature in the area must attempt a Reflex save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage, and any of its items with the tech trait become glitching 1 for 1 minute or until the condition is removed.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes double damage, and any of its items with the tech trait become glitching 2 for 1 minute or until the condition is removed.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d8.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"60-foot cone","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"paywall","n":"Paywall","fid":"CsLA3rJ9pwHb2loe","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You form a transparent wall of hardlight featuring payment terms in many languages. Each 10-foot-by-10-foot section of the wall has AC 10, Hardness 18, and 60 Hit Points, and its immune to critical hits and precision damage. The wall can be passed through by paying 10 credits and verifying the transaction as an single action with the auditory trait. Creatures that carry a credstick can pass, even if its empty, though in this case they pass through by taking on 10 credits of debt.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The Hit Points of each section of the wall increase by 15.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"60 feet","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"plant-form","n":"Plant Form","fid":"zCcfPS4y5SrZzU2x","t":["concentrate","manipulate","plant","polymorph","wood"],"lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"Taking inspiration from verdant creatures, you transform into a Large plant battle form. When you Cast this Spell, choose a listed battle form. You can substitute a similar specific plant to turn into (such as a pitcher plant instead of a flytrap), but this has no effect on the form's Size or statistics. While in this form, you gain the plant trait. You can Dismiss the spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which battle form you choose.\n\n- AC = 19 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n\n- 12 temporary Hit Points.\n\n- Resistance 10 to poison.\n\n- Low-light vision.\n\n- One or more unarmed melee attacks specific to the battle form you choose, which are the only attacks you can Strike with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +17, and your damage bonus is +11. These attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the Enfeebled condition, for example). If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead.\n\n- Athletics modifier of +19, unless your own modifier is higher.\n\nYou gain specific abilities based on the plant you choose.\n\n- **Moonflower**\n\nSpeed 30 feet;\n\n- Resistance 10 to electricity;\n\n- **Melee** ◆ bite (reach 15 feet), **Damage** 2d10 piercing;\n\n- **Melee** ◆ root (reach 15 feet), **Damage** 2d8 bludgeoning, and you can spend an action after a hit to Grab the target.\n\n- **Void Palm**\n\nSpeed 15 feet;\n\n- Resistance 10 to poison;\n\n- **Melee** ◆ void frond (reach 10 feet), **Damage** 2d8 slashing.\n\nPlant Form\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (6th)** Your battle form is Huge, and the reach of your attacks increases by 5 feet. You instead gain AC = 22 + your level, 24 temporary HP, attack modifier +21, damage bonus +16, and Athletics +22.","trad":["primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"prayermoji","n":"Prayermoji","fid":"7nzp5SwP5NoS3RRt","t":["concentrate","manipulate","sanctified","spirit"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You project an emoji of your deity's religious symbol around yourself. When you Cast the Spell and the first time you Sustain it on each subsequent turn, choose one of the following benefits depending on the emoji used.\n\n- **Prayer of Grace** You gain a +20-foot status bonus to your Speeds until the start of your next turn.\n\n- **Prayer of Healing** You regain 4 Hit Points at the start of your next turn.\n\n- **Prayer of Protection** You gain a +1 status bonus to AC and saving throws until the start of your next turn.\n\n- **Prayer of Retribution** Until the start of your next turn, creatures that hit you with melee Strikes take 4 spirit damage.\n\nPrayermoji\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The Hit Points regained increase by 1, and the spirit damage increases by 1.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"reflective-paneling","n":"Reflective Paneling","fid":"3iJb9h4yRGyIRzJd","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"The plates of your armor harden and become more reflective, enhanced with defensive magic. When you Cast this Spell, choose electricity, fire, piercing, or slashing damage. For the duration, you gain resistance 10 to that damage type and gain the Reflect Damage reaction.\n\nReflective Paneling\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (8th)** You can choose two damage types, and the resistance increases to 15. You can only Reflect Damage of one type at a time.\n\n**Heightened (10th)** As 8th, except the spell protects you against all four damage types, and the resistance increases to 20.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"rewire-flesh","n":"Rewire Flesh","fid":"0LQLmBrjK5B4mYQP","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You rewrite the target's DNA as if it was code, painfully warping its biological functions to mimic the processes of a robot: its body becomes visibly robotic as its blood vessels form circuit-like patterns, its bones twist into straight lines, its movements become jerky, and its voice grows halting. The target takes 3d6 slashing damage and 3d6 persistent bleed damage and must attempt a Will save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage and is Clumsy 1 for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage, is Clumsy 2 for 1 minute, and takes a –10-foot penalty to its Speeds for as long as it's clumsy.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the target takes double damage and is also Stupefied 1 for as long as it's clumsy.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The slashing damage and persistent bleed damage each increase by 1d6.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 living creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"subjective-reality","n":"Subjective Reality","fid":"CptKtBneM7od45nc","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You alter your perceptions to convince yourself that another creature or object is an illusion. Choose one object or creature you can perceive within range. For you, the target becomes transparent and doesn't create sound, smell, or other sensory output. You can move through the target, and the target can move through you. You gain resistance to all damage originating from the target equal to your level. If you are targeted by or are in the area of one of the target's abilities or effects, the target must succeed at a DC 5 flat check, and if it fails, you're unaffected by the ability or effect. You're immune to all of the target's auditory, linguistic, and scent-based attacks and effects. Your attacks deal no damage to the target, and the target is immune to your spells and other effects. You and the target can affect one another indirectly, such as through a Strike from a minion or through the environment affected by a witchwarper's quantum field. When this spell ends, the target becomes immune to subjective reality for 24 hours.\n\nSubjective Reality","trad":["occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"1","rng":"500 feet","tgt":"1 creature or object","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"summon-celestial","n":"Summon Celestial","fid":"lTDixrrNKaCvLKwX","t":["concentrate","manipulate","summon"],"lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You summon a creature that has the celestial trait and whose level is 5 or lower to fight for you. The GM might determine your deity restricts the specific types of celestials you can summon in certain cases.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened** As listed in the summon trait.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"30 feet","dur":"1 minute","sus":1},{"id":"summon-drift-prophet","n":"Summon Drift Prophet","fid":"IKzuw8XgMMw7ErSJ","t":["concentrate","incarnate","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You call forth a spectra tasked with monitoring the Drift and presenting its gift to technologically advanced civilizations. The spectra occupies the space of a Large creature, and has a Speed of 40 feet and a fly Speed of 60 feet with the cosmic trait.\n\n**Arrive** *Establish Universal Network* With a burst of divine energy from the Drift, the spectra restores (5*(item level - 1)) healing Hit Points to all creatures or objects with the tech trait within a 30-foot emanation and reduces their glitching condition by 5.\n\n**Depart** *Terminate Connection* Each creature or attended object with the tech trait within a 30-foot emanation must attempt a Fortitude save. On a failed save, the creature or object becomes Glitching 5, and creatures are Slowed 1 while they're glitching.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Increase the Hit Points restored by 5.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"5","rng":"100 feet","tgt":"until the end of your next turn","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"technological-combustion","n":"Technological Combustion","fid":"e65BnxbVVAMZ3Kqt","t":["concentrate","fire","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You rapidly overheat the systems of a technological weapon, causing it to expel a devastating wave of heat. If the target is held or worn, the creature holding or wielding it attempts a Reflex save. On a failure, or if the target is unattended, the target becomes Glitching 2, and all creatures within 20 feet of the target take 5d10 fire damage with a basic Reflex save.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d10.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 object or weapon with the tech trait","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"technophobia","n":"Technophobia","fid":"fs6YggxBweDzV3yG","t":["concentrate","emotion","fear","manipulate","mental"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You gather the message threads of thousands of angry technology users from the infosphere, making their pain a reality for your target whenever they use technology. The target must attempt a Will saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The first time each round the target uses a tech item, it takes 2d10 mental damage.\n\n**Failure** As success, but the target becomes Frightened 1 and takes 4d10 mental damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** As success, but the target becomes Frightened 2 and takes 8d10 mental damage.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"Will"},{"id":"wall-of-junk","n":"Wall of Junk","fid":"bTTakzdSo2S8fX92","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":5,"src":"TC","d":"You sculpt a barrier of trash that blocks sight and once broken, impedes foes. You create a 1-foot-thick wall of junk in either a hemisphere with a radius of 10 feet or a straight line up to 60 feet long and 10 feet high. The wall doesn't have to be vertical, but it must be anchored on both sides to a solid surface and can't pass through any creatures or objects, or the spell is lost.\n\nEach 10-foot-by-10-foot section of the wall has AC 10, Hardness 5, 20 Hit Points, and is immune to critical hits and precision damage. A destroyed section leaves behind a heap of jagged scrap that's difficult and hazardous terrain, dealing 2d6 slashing damage to a creature that enters the terrain for the first time on its turn.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The slashing damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"wave-of-warning","n":"Wave of Warning","fid":"kTzbLqmqPcZwOa5F","t":["concentrate","emotion","fear","manipulate","mental","nonlethal"],"lv":5,"src":"PC","d":"You deter enemies with a wave of hostile intent. The target takes 7d8 nonlethal mental damage, and the target must attempt a Will save. The psychic energy then arcs to another creature within 30 feet of the first target, jumps to another creature within 30 feet of that target, and so on. You can end the wave at any point. You can't target the same creature more than once, and you must have line of effect to all targets. Roll the damage only once, and apply it to each target (halving or doubling as appropriate for its saving throw outcome).\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target creature is unaffected, and the wave ends with that target.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is Frightened 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes double damage and is Frightened 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d8.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 creature, plus any number of additional creatures","save":"Will"},{"id":"corrosive-haze","n":"Corrosive Haze","fid":"nbIGKNr7eyiTqKwS","t":["acid","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You unleash a cloud of corrosive nanites. Creatures that start their turn in the area take 6d8 acid damage and 1d6 persistent acid damage with a basic Fortitude save. The nanites also corrode any unattended objects in the area, dealing 3d8 acid damage. Each round you Sustain the spell, you can move the cloud up to 10 feet in any direction. You can Dismiss the spell.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The initial damage increases by 1d8, and the persistent acid damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"20-foot burst","save":"basic Fortitude","sus":1},{"id":"dragon-form","n":"Dragon Form","fid":"5c692cCcTDXjSEzk","t":["concentrate","manipulate","polymorph"],"lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"Calling upon powerful magic, you gain a Large dragon battle form. When you Cast this Spell, choose one type of common dragon or another type to which your GM allows access. While in this form, you gain the dragon trait. You have hands in this battle form and can take manipulate actions. You can Dismiss the spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which battle form you choose:\n\n- AC = 18 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n\n- 10 temporary Hit Points.\n\n- Speed 40 feet, fly 100 feet. You gain any of the following Speeds the chosen dragon has, but with the listed amount: burrow 20 feet, climb 40 feet, swim 60 feet.\n\n- Resistance 10 against the damage type of your Dragon Breath (see below).\n\n- Darkvision and imprecise scent 60 feet.\n\n- The following unarmed melee attacks, which are the only attacks you can Strike with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +22, and your damage bonus is +6. These attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the enfeebled condition, for example). If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead. See below for more on these attacks.\n\n**Melee** ◆ jaws, **Damage** 2d12 piercing plus 2d6 damage of the same damage type as your Dragon Breath (see below);\n\n- **Melee** ◆ claw (agile), **Damage** 3d10 slashing;\n\n- **Melee** ◆ tail (reach 10 feet), **Damage** 3d10 bludgeoning.\n\n- Athletics modifier of +23, unless your own is higher.\n\n- **Dragon Breath** ◆◆ You exhale deadly magical energy in an area, dealing 10d6 damage to each creature in the area with a basic save against your spell DC. The shape, damage type, and save type match that of your chosen dragon's breath. If the chosen dragon's breath can deal more than one type of damage, choose one when you cast *dragon form*. The shape is a 30-foot cone or a 100-foot line. Once activated, Dragon Breath can't be used again for 1d4 rounds. Dragon Breath has the tradition trait matching the type of dragon and the damage trait matching the type of damage it deals, if applicable.\n\n- **Tradition Resistance** If the dragon's magical tradition matches that of your dragon form spell, you gain the listed ability. **Arcane** resistance 5 against magic; **divine** resistance 10 to spirit, vitality, and void; **occult** resistance 10 to mental; **primal** resistance 5 to physical damage.\n\nDragon Form\n\n| Dragon | Tradition | Speeds | Dragon Breath | Saving Throw |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Abysium | Arcane | — | Cone of poison | Fortitude |\n| Akashic | Occult | — | Cone of mental | Will |\n| Cosmic | Divine | — | Cone of spirit | Will |\n| Host | Primal | Climb | Cone of piercing | Reflex |\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (8th)** Your battle form is Huge, you gain a +20-foot status bonus to your fly Speed, and your attacks have 10-foot reach (or 15-foot reach if they previously had 10-foot reach). You instead gain AC = 21 + your level, 15 temporary HP, an attack modifier of +28, a damage bonus of +12, and Athletics +28. Your Dragon Breath deals an additional 4d6 damage.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"explosive-recall","n":"Explosive Recall","fid":"7o0Fbp7CsocbKSab","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"TC","d":"You capture and repeat the memory of a grenade's explosion within its shell. If you Area-Fire with the locus during the duration of the spell, the grenade's effect is repeated in the same area 1 round after the initial activation.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"pocket-vacuum","n":"Pocket Vacuum","fid":"ITzIb93GBvyX8UbJ","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You create a sudden vacuum, forcing creatures in the area to hold their breath or fall Unconscious and start suffocating. The explosive decompression deals 5d12 bludgeoning damage to each creature in the area when the spell is cast or that enters the area during the duration (unless they were already in a vacuum), with a basic Fortitude save. Creatures who critically fail the save are also knocked Prone.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d12.","trad":["arcane","divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"20-foot burst","save":"basic Fortitude"},{"id":"promession","n":"Promession","fid":"xS4bqHnbodCwjpqI","t":["attack","cold","concentrate","death","manipulate","sonic"],"lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You flash freeze a target then send subsonic waves through it, potentially reducing it into fine powder. Make a spell attack against the target. If you hit a target, the target takes 6d8 cold damage and must attempt a Fortitude save. If you critically hit, the target gets a result one degree of success worse than it rolled on its Fortitude save. A creature reduced to 0 Hit Points is blasted to fine powder; its gear remains.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected by further damage.\n\n**Success** The target takes an additional ((item level -3)d8) sonic damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes an additional ((item level)d8) sonic damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes an additional ((item level +6)d8) sonic damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The cold and sonic damage each increase by 1d8.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 creature or unattended object","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"raise-dead","n":"Raise Dead","fid":"IkGYwHRLhkuoGReG","t":["concentrate","healing","manipulate"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You attempt to call forth the dead creature's soul, requiring the creature's body to be present and relatively intact. The creature must have died within the past 3 days. If Pharasma has decided that the creature's time has come (at the GM's discretion), or if the creature doesn't wish to return to life, this spell automatically fails, but the cost isn't consumed in the casting.\n\nIf the spell is successful, the creature returns to life with 1 Hit Point, no spells prepared or spell slots available, no points in any pools or any other daily resources, and still with any long-term debilitations of the old body. The time spent in the Boneyard leaves the target temporarily debilitated, making it Clumsy 2, Drained 2, and Enfeebled 2 for 1 week; these conditions can't be removed or reduced by any means until the week has passed. The creature is also permanently changed by its time in the afterlife, such as a slight personality shift, a streak of white in the hair, or a strange new birthmark.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (7th)** The maximum level of the target increases to 15. The cost increases to the target's level (minimum 1) × 4,000 credits.\n\n**Heightened (8th)** The maximum level of the target increases to 17. The cost increases to the target's level (minimum 1) × 8,000 credits.\n\n**Heightened (9th)** The maximum level of the target increases to 19. The cost increases to the target's level (minimum 1) × 16,000 credits.\n\n**Heightened (10th)** The maximum level of the target increases to 21. The cost increases to the target's level (minimum 1) × 32,000 credits.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"10 minutes","rng":"10 feet","tgt":"1 dead creature of 13th level or lower","cost":"gemstones worth a total value of the target's level (minimum 1) × 2,000 credits"},{"id":"rocket-dash","n":"Rocket Dash","fid":"BHWG0rQPTgBF5Ye1","t":["concentrate","fire","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You emit a rocket of flame from behind you and blast forward. You move in a straight line up to twice your Speed; you can move through spaces occupied by creatures, and the movement doesn't trigger reactions. Creatures in the area take 6d12 fire damage with a basic Reflex save. On a critical failure, a creature also takes 2d6 persistent fire damage and is Dazzled for 1 round. You reappear at the end of the line.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The fire damage increases by 2d12, and the persistent fire damage on a critical failure increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"shield-wall","n":"Shield Wall","fid":"i4KJpgO0nv6TY73L","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"TC","d":"You magnify the protective power of your shield, slamming it into the ground and causing it to grow into a wall up to 60 feet long, 30 feet high, and 1/4 inch thick. The wall is made of the same material as the locus and doesn't need to stand vertically, forming a straight line parallel to the shield's surface. If the wall would pass through a creature or object, the spell is lost. Each 10-foot-by-10-foot section of the wall has AC 10, is immune to critical hits and precision damage, and has the same Hardness, HP, and BT as the locus. Creatures can move through a section of the wall that's broken.","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"slice-reality","n":"Slice Reality","fid":"a02hsymtiVRQvh3i","t":["concentrate","manipulate","void"],"lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You slice through reality, forming a chasm of life-draining entropy in a straight line 20 feet high, 120 feet long, and 2 inches thick. The chasm provides cover. The chasm deals 7d8 void damage to each creature that's in the chasm's space when it's created, that attempts to pass through the chasm, or that ends its turn inside the chasm, with a basic Reflex save. A creature that succeeds at this save when the chasm is created is pushed to the nearest space on the side of its choice. Creatures trying to move through the chasm fail to do so if they critically fail the save, ending their movement next to the chasm.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d8.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"spark-of-the-spirit","n":"Spark of the Spirit","fid":"S1nvwfmweG4AEGGW","t":["concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"TC","d":"You create a sphere of spiritual electricity. Each ally that begins their turn in the area is Quickened and can use this additional action only to Interact or Step. Allies quickened in this way immediately regain all charges on batteries in their possession and deal an additional 3d4 electricity damage when they Strike with a tech weapon.\n\nSpark of the Spirit","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"20-foot burst"},{"id":"telekinetic-strangulation","n":"Telekinetic Strangulation","fid":"OudLZtxmg6gI1UEL","t":["attack","concentrate","incapacitation","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You telekinetically grasp a creature's throat or similar vital anatomy with a vicelike grip, forcefully lifting it a few inches off the ground as it struggles to breathe. Make a ranged spell attack against the target's AC. On a hit, you deal 6d12 bludgeoning damage, and the target is Immobilized. While immobilized in this way, it must hold its breath or begin suffocating. The first time each round you Sustain the spell, the target takes 1d12 bludgeoning damage, remains immobilized, and must continue holding its breath. The target can attempt to Escape (the Escape DC is your spell DC, and the attempt is affected by the incapacitation trait).","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"wall-of-coiling-lightning","n":"Wall of Coiling Lightning","fid":"vgagfjqR9N572poC","t":["concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"TC","d":"You create 20-foot-tall metal coils that harness the power of electricity, arcing current between two unoccupied spaces up to 30 feet apart. These coils each have AC 10, 60 Hit Points, and are immune to critical hits and precision damage. The spell ends if either coil is destroyed. A constant stream of electricity flows between these coils in a visible, straight line. Creatures can see and move through the coils; however, if a creature enters or starts its turn in the stream of electricity or within 5 feet of a coil, it takes 4d12 electricity damage with a basic Reflex save. On a failed save, the target is also Off-Guard for 1 round.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+2)** The damage increases by 1d12.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","dur":"1 minute","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"wall-of-plasma","n":"Wall of Plasma","fid":"dRP4Imw3RJNQqEgc","t":["concentrate","electricity","fire","manipulate"],"lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You shape a wall of crackling plasma that burns creatures passing through it. You create either a 5-foot-thick wall of plasma in a straight line up to 60 feet long and 10 feet high, or a 5-foot-thick, 10-foot-radius ring of plasma with the same height. The wall stands vertically in either form; if you wish, the wall can be of a shorter length or height. Everything on each side of the wall is Concealed from creatures on the opposite side. Any creature that crosses the wall or is occupying the wall's area at the start of its turn takes 4d6 fire damage and 2d6 persistent electricity damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The persistent electricity damage increases by 1d6.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"x-ray-vision","n":"X-Ray Vision","fid":"DPP4TW5FxE85XPKZ","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"r":"u","lv":6,"src":"PC","d":"You empower yourself to see through most materials and walls within 60 feet. Your sight is blocked by 2 feet of wood or plastic, 1 foot of stone, 2 inches of common metal, or any amount of lead or any starmetal, and you can only see in black and white.","trad":["arcane","divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"absolute-zero","n":"Absolute Zero","fid":"kGas0LdEAR1WjLGZ","t":["cold","concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":7,"src":"PC","d":"A swirling vortex flash freezes the air, dealing 10d8 cold damage. Each creature in the area must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is Slowed 1 until the start of your next turn.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, is Immobilized by a layer of ice, and is slowed 1 as long as it's immobilized. The ice is an object with 50 Hit Points, Hardness 5, immunity to cold damage, and vulnerability 10 to fire. It has object immunities and is destroyed if the target Escapes.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d8 and the ice's Hit Points increase by 5.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"500 feet","area":"30-foot burst","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"boot-loop","n":"Boot Loop","fid":"qwVddukwlfbtm1Ti","t":["auditory","concentrate","manipulate","sonic"],"lv":7,"src":"TC","d":"You deliver a perfectly crafted command with the power of your voice, triggering mass reboots and shaking bodies apart. You deal 10d8 sonic damage to all creatures in the area. Each creature must attempt a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage. Creatures with the tech trait become Glitching 1, and creatures without the tech trait are Deafened for 1 round.\n\n**Critical Failure** The target takes double damage. Creatures with the tech trait become Glitching 2, and creatures without the tech trait are deafened for 1 minute.","trad":[],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"60-foot cone","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"death-sentence","n":"Death Sentence","fid":"zdzeVZlKHkMAt2Rf","t":["auditory","concentrate","death","incapacitation","spirit"],"lv":7,"src":"PC","d":"You draw a line of universal condemnation and judge the target unfit to exist. The target takes 11d10 spirit damage with a basic Will save. On a failure, the creature also believes it's been imprisoned as it awaits punishment and becomes Paralyzed for 1 round (or paralyzed for 2 rounds on a critical failure).\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d10.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"1 creature","save":"basic Will"},{"id":"emoji-tsunami","n":"Emoji Tsunami","fid":"EsmK1lCqW9wjGXHh","t":["concentrate","force","manipulate","water"],"lv":7,"src":"TC","d":"You unleash a wave of emojis. Creatures in the area take 13d6 bludgeoning damage and must attempt a Reflex saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and is pushed 10 feet away from you. This is forced movement.\n\n**Failure** As success, but the creature takes full damage and is also knocked Prone.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the creature takes double damage and is also Blinded for 1 minute by lingering water droplet emojis.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 2d6.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"60-foot cone","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"howl","n":"Howl","fid":"g9QLswd5uqDdcCjv","t":["auditory","concentrate","manipulate","mental","sonic"],"lv":7,"src":"PC","d":"You let out a powerful ululation full of psychic resonance that compels others who hear it to join in. You deal 7d12 sonic damage and 1d8 persistent mental damage to other creatures who can hear within the area. Targets must attempt a Will save. The persistent mental damage a creature takes from this spell increases by 1d8 if at least one other creature is howling. A howling creature can't use auditory actions or cast spells except for those with the subtle trait for 1 round. Calculate the persistent damage after all creatures attempt their saves.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage and no persistent mental damage.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage, persistent mental damage, and is compelled to howl as long as it takes persistent mental damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, but the target takes double the initial and persistent damage.","trad":["divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","area":"30-foot emanation","save":"Will"},{"id":"judgment-cannon","n":"Judgment Cannon","fid":"onJigrID4TH48kag","t":["concentrate","manipulate","sanctified","spirit"],"lv":7,"src":"TC","d":"You create a ghostly, semi-corporeal turret made of divine force in an unoccupied space in range. The turret is Medium; creatures can move through the turret's space but can't end their movement in it. When you Cast the Spell and the first time you Sustain it each turn on subsequent rounds, the turret fires, dealing 8d8 spirit damage to all creatures in a 60- foot line originating from the turret (basic Reflex save).\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The damage increases by 1d8.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"60 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"60-foot line","save":"basic Reflex","sus":1},{"id":"root-of-all-pain","n":"Root of all Pain","fid":"ZhQWnQ0500AAtjDb","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental","plant"],"lv":7,"src":"PC","d":"Your finger pushes a tiny root into the target's body that begins to grow, burrowing through the nervous system as it feeds off the electric signals triggered by the agonizing pain of its intrusive spread. The target attempts a Fortitude save.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The target takes 2d8 mental damage the first time each round it performs any action other than an action that is purely mental, such as Recall Knowledge (or other actions as determined by the GM).\n\n**Failure** As success, except the target takes 4d8 mental damage and is Slowed 1 for the duration of the spell.\n\n**Critical Failure** As success, except the target takes 6d8 mental damage and is Slowed 2 for the duration of the spell.","trad":["primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","dur":"1 minute","save":"Fortitude"},{"id":"void-scour","n":"Void Scour","fid":"x21WInzhprQHMyKT","t":["concentrate","darkness","manipulate","void"],"lv":7,"src":"PC","d":"A well of desolate darkness scours all life, dealing 10d10 void damage to all living creatures in the area. Each creature in the area must attempt a Reflex save. If void scour overlaps with an area of magical light or affects a creature affected by magical light, void scour attempts to counteract the light effect.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and (rank - 6)d6 persistent void damage, and becomes Drained 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and (rank - 5)d6 persistent void damage, and becomes Drained 2.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** Increase the initial void damage by 2d10. The persistent void damage increases by 1d6 on a failure, or by 2d6 on critical failure.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"500 feet","area":"60-foot burst","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"wall-of-steel","n":"Wall of Steel","fid":"fRT0T9sbd8zWc1q9","t":["concentrate","manipulate","metal"],"lv":7,"src":"PC","d":"You shape a wall of solid steel. You create a 4-inch-thick wall of steel up to 120 feet long and 20 feet high. You can shape the wall's path, placing each 5 feet of the wall on the border between squares. The wall doesn't need to stand vertically, so you can use it to form a bridge or set of stairs, for example. You must conjure the wall in an unbroken open space so its edges don't pass through any creatures or objects, or the spell is lost.\n\nEach 10-foot-by-10-foot section of the wall has AC 10, Hardness 18, and 60 Hit Points, and it's immune to critical hits and precision damage. A destroyed section of the wall can be moved through, but the rubble created from it is difficult terrain.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The Hit Points of each section of the wall increase by 15.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"akashic-revival","n":"Akashic Revival","fid":"f98vwzcdxafum8ln","t":["concentrate","exploration","manipulate"],"lv":8,"src":"PC","d":"You dispatch perfect documentation of the target's physical body to the Akashic Record, allowing it to later recall this record and reconstruct its body as it was when you cast this spell. The record includes the target's current Hit Points, augmentations, attribute modifiers, and any afflictions or conditions it had.\n\nIf the target dies of anything other than old age, it can recall its recorded body from the Akashic Record. This process takes 1 minute, after which time its corpse disappears, and the target instantly reappears in the recorded body in the corpse's space and with any worn equipment. It re-forms standing and can choose to pick up any equipment it dropped in the space from when it died, assuming the equipment is still there. If it can't occupy that space, it appears as close to the space as possible, though it must still retrieve its equipment. It retains its mind as it was at the time of the body's death, so it regains no expended spells, Focus Points, or uses of special abilities. Any mental effects affecting the target at the time of its death persist in its new body.\n\nRetrieving the body from the Akashic Record or having the duration expire removes the stored information from the Akashic Record, requiring you to cast this spell again.\n\nCasting the spell replaces any previous record you've stored with prior castings—you can store only one copy of any creature in the Akashic Record using this spell.","trad":["occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"10 minutes","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 willing creature","dur":"1 day"},{"id":"disappearance","n":"Disappearance","fid":"wfleiawxsfhpRRwf","t":["illusion","manipulate","subtle"],"lv":8,"src":"PC","d":"You shroud a creature from others' senses. The target becomes Undetected, not just to sight but to all senses, allowing the target to count as Invisible no matter what precise and imprecise senses an observer might have. It's still possible for a creature to find the target by Seeking, looking for disturbed dust, hearing gaps in the sound spectrum, or finding some other way to discover the presence of an otherwise-undetectable creature.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 creature","dur":"10 minutes"},{"id":"divine-firewall","n":"Divine Firewall","fid":"WzROOMfaK77OMgjB","t":["concentrate","holy","manipulate"],"lv":8,"src":"TC","d":"You fill the space around you with divine flames that protect allies within it and burn away those who mean you harm, especially from unholy and technological threats. You and allies in the area are Concealed. As the nature of this effect still leaves the target's location obvious, the target can't use this concealment to [[/act hide]] or [[/act sneak]].\n\nEnemies beginning their turn in the area take 10 fire damage, become Glitching 1 if they have the tech trait, and become Off-Guard for 1 round if they have the unholy trait.","trad":["divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute","area":"60-foot emanation"},{"id":"flight-of-the-lightning-bees","n":"Flight of the Lightning Bees","fid":"6IAcZLBCv4SECaFU","t":["concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"lv":8,"src":"TC","d":"**Area** up to 4 non-overlapping 20-foot bursts\n\nBeelike elementals made of pure electricity swarm out of countless portals. When you Cast the Spell and the first time you Sustain the spell each subsequent round, creatures in the area take 6d12 piercing damage and 3d6 persistent electricity damage and must attempt a Fortitude save. The first time you Sustain the spell each subsequent round, you can also move one of the bursts 15 feet in any direction, though you can't move bursts so they overlap.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and is Suppressed for 1 round.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and is suppressed for as long as it takes the persistent damage.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage and is suppressed and Clumsy 2 for as long as it takes the persistent damage.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (+1)** The piercing damage increases by 1d12.","trad":["occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"20-foot burst","save":"Will"},{"id":"gravity-field","n":"Gravity Field","fid":"gLOelTMvex2OgBqV","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":8,"src":"PC","d":"Bending the laws of the Universe to your will, you increase the forces of gravity in an area. All flying creatures in the area descend 40 feet. The entire area is greater difficult terrain for Flying and Climbing creatures, and difficult terrain for creatures on the ground. Any creature pulled to the ground by a gravity field takes bludgeoning damage as though it had fallen.\n\nGravity in the area increases by one step (for example, zero-g becomes low gravity, low gravity becomes standard, standard gravity becomes high gravity, and high gravity becomes extreme gravity).","trad":["arcane","divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"100 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"30-foot cylinder","sus":1},{"id":"monstrosity-form","n":"Monstrosity Form","fid":"8AMvNVOUEtxBCDvJ","t":["concentrate","manipulate","polymorph"],"lv":8,"src":"PC","d":"You transform into the shape of a legendary monster, assuming a Huge battle form. When you Cast this Spell, choose dust manta, nyssholora, or space worm. While in one of these forms, you gain the beast trait. You can Dismiss the spell.\n\nYou gain the following statistics and abilities regardless of which battle form you choose.\n\n- AC = 20 + your level. Ignore your armor's check penalty and Speed reduction.\n- 20 temporary Hit Points.\n- Darkvision.\n- One or more unarmed melee attacks specific to the battle form you choose, which are the only attacks you can Strike with. You're trained with them. Your attack modifier is +28, and you use the listed damage. These attacks are Strength based (for the purpose of the Enfeebled condition, for example). If your unarmed attack modifier is higher, you can use it instead.\n- Athletics modifier of +30, unless your own is higher.\nYou gain specific abilities based on the monster you choose:\n\n- **Dust Manta**\n\nSpeed 15 feet, burrow 40 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ stinger (agile, finesse, reach 15 feet), **Damage** 2d6+12 piercing plus 4d4 persistent poison;\n- **Burrowing Charge** ◆◆ (move) You Burrow up to twice your burrow Speed, then Leap vertically up to 25 feet high, making a stinger Strike against a creature at any point during the jump. After the Leap, you fall to the ground, but take no damage from the fall if you land on dirt or sand.\n\n- **Nyssholora**\n\nSpeed 40 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ jaws (reach 10 feet), **Damage** 2d12+20 piercing;\n- **Melee** ◆ phasic blade (razing, reach 15 feet), **Damage** 2d10+13 sonic plus phasic strike;\n- **Ranged** ◆ tail scourge discharge (range increment 120 feet), **Damage** 7d6 electricity;\n- **Phasic Flurry** ◆◆◆ (move, traversal) You Stride up to your Speed, then make a phasic blade Strike against each creature within reach. Each attack counts toward your multiple attack penalty, but don't increase the penalty until all these attacks have been made;\n- **Phasic Strike** Your phasic blade Strikes treat any object or construct they hit as if it had half as much Hardness as usual.\n\n- **Space Worm**\n\nSpeed 40 feet, burrow 40 feet, swim 40 feet;\n- **Melee** ◆ jaws (reach 15 feet), **Damage** 2d12+20 piercing;\n- **Melee** ◆ tongue (finesse, reach 30 feet), **Effect** tongue grab; A creature hit by your tongue becomes Grabbed by you. The creature isn't Immobilized, but it can't move beyond the reach of your tongue. A creature can sever the tongue with a Strike against your AC that deals at least 30 slashing damage. This deals no damage to you but prevents you from using your tongue Strike until you regrow your tongue, such as by casting the spell again later.\n\nMonstrosity Form\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (9th)** You instead gain AC = 22 + your level, 25 temporary HP, attack modifier +31, increase damage by one damage die, and Athletics +33.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","dur":"1 minute"},{"id":"phantasmal-fleet","n":"Phantasmal Fleet","fid":"Y3egStSTzL8k86qc","t":["concentrate","illusion","manipulate","mental"],"lv":8,"src":"PC","d":"A menacing vision of a fleet of hostile starships fills the mind of each creature in the area. The ships appear to be 1,000 feet overhead bombarding the ground with laser fire. The vision deals 10d8 mental damage with a basic Will save. On a critical failure, the target also believes it's being pursued and moves to take cover. It must spend an action to Take Cover on each of its turns, which may require it to first move to a new space or Drop Prone. It can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of its turns, and on a success, it disbelieves the phantasm and stops being forced to Take Cover.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"500 feet","area":"60-foot burst","save":"Will"},{"id":"singularity-seed","n":"Singularity Seed","fid":"aPZMapuunaNpxubp","t":["concentrate","manipulate","void"],"lv":8,"src":"PC","d":"A tiny particle of incredibly dense mass magically blossoms into a gravitational singularity that pulls creatures toward it and spatially compresses any creatures that are moved into it. You create a singularity in a 5-foot square that is unoccupied by any creatures. All creatures and unsecured objects in a 50-foot emanation around the singularity are moved toward the singularity when the spell is cast, depending on their Reflex save (see below). Creatures and objects are moved starting with those closest to the singularity, so they might block the path of other creatures and objects that are pulled in later.\n\nCreatures' spaces can overlap in the square that contains the singularity. A creature or object that enters the singularity or ends its turn there takes 10d10 bludgeoning damage with no saving throw. While in the singularity, a creature can take no actions except to attempt to Escape against your Spell DC. When the spell ends, the singularity disappears, and overlapping creatures are moved to the closest unoccupied space, as determined by the GM.\n\nSquares in the emanation are difficult terrain for creatures moving away from the singularity, and creatures moving toward the singularity can move 10 feet for each 5 feet of movement they spend.\n\nA creature needs to attempt a Reflex save if it's in the area when the spell is cast and when it ends its turn in the area.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature is pulled 10 feet toward the singularity.\n\n**Failure** The creature is pulled 20 feet toward the singularity.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature is pulled 30 feet toward the singularity.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"100 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"5-foot square","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"transfer-consciousness","n":"Transfer Consciousness","fid":"iPfHkWGAwocCqU1E","t":["concentrate","manipulate","possession"],"lv":8,"src":"TC","d":"You project your mind into an advanced piece of technology, allowing you to interact with its systems as if they were your own body. The target's level must be equal to or lower than your own. Your own body is helpless and falls Prone as if you were Unconscious. At the end of the spell, your mind returns to your body instantly as long as your body and the target are on the same plane. Otherwise, the spell becomes permanent, and your real body enters a coma.\n\nWhile your mind is in a computer, for 1 hour, you can roll your spell attack modifier instead of Computers for Computers skill actions related to that system, and you can attempt trained Computers skill actions even if you're untrained.\n\nWhile your mind is in a construct, you have access to its physical functions, allowing you to control it as if it was your own body for 1 minute. You can use any special actions the construct has access to, though you can't cast its spells, if any. You can cast your own spells using the construct's body.","trad":["occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"touch","tgt":"1 willing computer or tech construct","dur":"varies"},{"id":"void-vessel","n":"Void Vessel","fid":"sTpdXXaaKhoGOIxh","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":8,"src":"PC","d":"You grant creatures the ability to survive in a vacuum. Targeted creatures gain the cosmic trait and sprout wings of shimmering energy that grant a fly Speed of 30 feet. The wings function only in a vacuum.\n\nVoid Vessel","trad":["divine","occult","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"30 feet","tgt":"you and up to 10 willing creatures","dur":"8 hours"},{"id":"atomic-blast","n":"Atomic Blast","fid":"UnWaP06SVi3jRN0M","t":["concentrate","fire","manipulate","radiation"],"lv":9,"src":"PC","d":"You magically split an atom, creating an explosion with radioactive fallout. All creatures in the area take 5d12 bludgeoning damage and 5d12 fire damage, and they're exposed to extreme radiation that uses your spellcasting DC as the Fortitude DC for radiation sickness incurred by exposure to this radiation. The onset and frequency of this magical radiation is 1 round, and the area remains radioactive for 10 minutes.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected by the initial damage.\n\n**Success** The target takes half damage and is Dazzled for 1 minute.\n\n**Failure** The target takes full damage and is Blinded for 1 minute.\n\n**Critical Failure** As failure, and the target takes double damage.","trad":["arcane","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"500 feet","area":"100-foot burst","save":"Reflex"},{"id":"call-cosmos","n":"Call Cosmos","fid":"J3zMwmhIVgI2yzxm","t":["cold","concentrate","fire","manipulate"],"lv":9,"src":"PC","d":"You reach into the void and call down a vertical column of dangerous cosmic material that rains destruction upon creatures in the area and shrouds the terrain around it in a swirl of stardust. This matter is made up of bits of burning stars and chunks of frozen comets, and it deals 5d12 cold damage and 5d12 fire damage to every creature in the area when you Cast the Spell. For the spell's duration, the cosmic material reduces visibility and mobility, making the area greater difficult terrain and making everything seen within or through the area Concealed.\n\n---\n\n**Heightened (10th)** The cold and fire damage each increase by 2d12.","trad":["divine","primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"500 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"20-foot cylinder","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"kill-dash-nine","n":"Kill Dash Nine","fid":"SrgvGhssLCzzhiNo","t":["concentrate","manipulate"],"lv":9,"src":"TC","d":"You send a brutal signal interruption straight into the central processor of a technological being. This signal wreaks havoc on the system and leaves behind lasting corruption. The target takes 15d8 mental damage, or electricity damage, if the target is immune to mental damage. Beings that are biomechanical (such as androids) or only partially mechanical (such as cyborgs) uses the outcome for one degree of success better than the result of their saving throw.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The creature is unaffected.\n\n**Success** The creature takes half damage and becomes Glitching 1.\n\n**Failure** The creature takes full damage and becomes Glitching 2 and Stunned 1.\n\n**Critical Failure** The creature takes double damage, becomes Glitching 3 and Stunned 2, and must succeed at a Fortitude save or suffer catastrophic systems failure. This kills any creature reliant on technology to live. This Fortitude save has the death and incapacitation traits.","trad":["divine","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 creature with the tech trait","save":"Will"},{"id":"mycorrhizal-supremacy","n":"Mycorrhizal Supremacy","fid":"LcAzycyG5Tqk92Bx","t":["concentrate","incapacitation","manipulate","mental","plant"],"r":"u","lv":9,"src":"TC","d":"You create a network of mind-controlling mycotoxins directly in targets' brains, attempting to seize command and force them to obey you. The first target must attempt a Will save. If it doesn't critically succeed, another target within 30 feet of the first attempts a Will save; if that target doesn't critically succeed, another target within 30 feet of it attempts a Will save, and so on. You can choose to end the spread at any point, and you can't target the same creature more than once. Once the spell has taken effect, you can only focus on one member of the network to control at a time. You can change the target of your focus by Sustaining the spell.\n\n---\n\n**Critical Success** The target is unaffected, and your network can spread no farther.\n\n**Success** The target is Stunned 1 as it fights off your spores.\n\n**Failure** The target joins your mycorrhizal network. It gains the Controlled condition but can act normally unless it's the focus of your control. If it's the focus, it can attempt a Will save at the end of each of its turns. On a success, the target drops out of the network, and your focus automatically shifts to the closest remaining member of the network.\n\n**Critical Failure** As a failure, but the target receives a new save only if you give it a new order that's against its nature, such as killing its allies.","trad":["primal"],"cat":"spell","time":"2","rng":"120 feet","tgt":"1 living creature (see text below)","dur":"until your next daily preparations","save":"Will"},{"id":"summon-giant-robot","n":"Summon Giant Robot","fid":"UDhfM3MWs5yAsCvx","t":["concentrate","incarnate","manipulate"],"lv":9,"src":"TC","d":"You call forth a titanic robot. The robot occupies the space of a Huge creature, and has a Speed of 80 feet and a fly Speed of 100 feet with the cosmic trait.\n\n**Arrive** *Ultra Cannon Onslaught* (traversal) The robot Strides once in a straight line, trampling enemies underfoot to deal 10d8 bludgeoning damage (basic Reflex save). It then unleashes a volley of lasers from its chest in a 60-foot cone or 120-foot line, which can't overlap with the area of the its Stride, dealing 10d8 force damage (basic Reflex save).\n\n**Depart** *Missile Silo* Unleashed The robot fires rockets at up to 8 different creatures up to 120 feet away, dealing 9d8 fire damage (basic Reflex save).","trad":["arcane","divine"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"100 feet","dur":"until the end of your next turn","save":"basic Reflex"},{"id":"telekinetic-tantrum","n":"Telekinetic Tantrum","fid":"64DDZxOrmr4ddqs2","t":["attack","concentrate","force","manipulate"],"lv":9,"src":"PC","d":"You launch a barrage of powerful psychokinetic energy that overpowers creatures, hurls objects, and deals damage. When you Cast this Spell and the first time each round you Sustain the spell, you can choose one of the following effects. You can't choose the same effect twice in a row.\n\n- **Back Off!** You hurl up to 15 objects or creatures up to 40 feet in any direction (including up or down). You can hurl up to a total weight of 40 Bulk per creature or object. Creatures take bludgeoning damage based on the distance they moved and land Prone, as though they'd taken falling damage. Creatures that succeed on a Fortitude save against the spell avoid being moved.\n- **Hard Rain** You pummel all creatures in the area with debris and objects in the area, dealing 5d10 bludgeoning damage with a basic Reflex save.\n- **Psychokinetic Slam** Your psychokinetic storm slams into all creatures in the area. Make a ranged spell attack roll. All targets you hit take 7d6 force damage and are Stunned 1.","trad":["arcane","occult"],"cat":"spell","time":"3","rng":"500 feet","dur":"1 minute","area":"100-foot burst","sus":1}]; })(typeof window !== "undefined" ? window : globalThis);
